"command":"python3 <<'PY'\nimport json, subprocess\nfor id in [\"MARATHON-2\",\"MARATHON-3\",\"MARATHON-4\",\"MARATHON-5\",\"MARATHON-6\",\"MARATHON-7\",\"MARATHON-8\",\"MARATHON-9\",\"MARATHON-10\",\"MARATHON-11\"]:\n    out = subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"show\",id,\"--output\",\"json\"], text=True)\n    # strip log lines\n    start = out.find(\"{\")\n    d = json.loads(out[start:])\n    print(\"=\"*60)\n    print(d[\"id\"], d[\"title\"])\n    print(\"labels:\", d.get(\"labels\"))\n    print(\"priority:\", d.get(\"priority\"))\n    print(\"desc:\", d.get(\"description\"))\n    print(\"has_design:\", d.get(\"has_design\"))\n# list all\nout = subprocess.check_output([\"loom\",\"data\",\"list\",\"--parent\",\"MARATHON-1\",\"--output\",\"json\"], text=True)\nstart = out.find(\"[\")\nitems = json.loads(out[start:])\nprint(\"\\nTOTAL CHILDREN:\", len(items))\nfor i in items:\n    print(i[\"id\"], i[\"title\"], \"labels=\", i.get(\"labels\"))\nPY","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"============================================================\nMARATHON-2 Bootstrap cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis, health\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 0\ndesc: Implement /app/start.sh that stays in the foreground, launches Redis on 127.0.0.1:6379, and three HTTP nodes on :8000/:8001/:8002. Auto-respawn killed HTTP nodes within 60s and Redis after kill. GET /api/health on each node returns 200 {status:ok, node_id} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports. Self-contained; no remote services or Docker-in-Docker.\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-3 Auth: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 0\ndesc: Implement POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me per API contract. Username slug rules, password >=8, 201/200 envelopes {user,token} or {user}, 400/401/409 as specified. Token length >=16. Shared durable store across all three nodes.\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-4 Profiles: GET user and PATCH /api/users/me\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 1\ndesc: UserObj fields {id,username,display_name,timezone,avatar_url,status_text,status_emoji}. GET /api/users/{id} → 200/404. PATCH /api/users/me accepts subset, validates timezone/lengths → 400. Profile updates broadcast WS user.updated globally (hook up when WS exists).\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-5 Workspaces: create, list, detail, members, roles, ownership\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 0\ndesc: POST/GET/PATCH workspaces per contract. Auto-create #general; creator is owner. join_mode open|invite_only. Members list, role PATCH rules (owner/admin/member/guest), transfer_ownership. Open-workspace join semantics and role-based channel create permissions as specified.\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-6 Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, members\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 0\ndesc: ChannelObj, POST workspace channels, join/leave, PATCH topic, archive/unarchive (owner-only), members list. Private vs public rules, guest restrictions, archived writes → 423. Duplicate name → 409. Topic max 250.\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-7 Messages: post, list, edit, delete with pagination\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 0\ndesc: POST/GET channel messages, PATCH/DELETE message. Empty body → 400. MessageObj shape including author, files, reactions, mentions placeholders. Newest-first pagination ?limit=&before=. Edit sets edited_at; delete idempotent; edit deleted → 409.\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-8 Threads: replies endpoint and reply_count\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 1\ndesc: Support parent_id on message create. GET /api/messages/{parent_id}/replies oldest-first. Parent reply_count bumps. Thread replies participate in durable channel seq when WS is wired.\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-9 Reactions and pins on messages\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 1\ndesc: POST/DELETE reactions; aggregate {emoji,count,user_ids}; idempotent per user+emoji. Pin POST/DELETE and GET channel pins newest-first; private non-members → 403 on pin list.\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-10 DMs: get-or-create pairwise channel\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 1\ndesc: POST /api/dms {user_id} returns 200 {channel_id}; same id both directions and on repeat. Channel marked is_dm.\nhas_design: False\n============================================================\nMARATHON-11 Files: upload, metadata, download, attach to messages\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\npriority: 1\ndesc: POST /api/files multipart, GET metadata, GET download with Content-Type/Disposition. >10MiB → 413. file_ids on message create must be caller's own and unattached else 400.\nhas_design: False\n\nTOTAL CHILDREN: 18\nMARATHON-2 Bootstrap cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis, health labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nMARATHON-3 Auth: register, login, me, bearer tokens labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nMARATHON-5 Workspaces: create, list, detail, members, roles, ownership labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nMARATHON-6 Channels: create, join, leave, topic, archive, members labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nMARATHON-7 Messages: post, list, edit, delete with pagination labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nMARATHON-18 WebSocket subscribe, resume, dense per-channel seq labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nMARATHON-19 Cluster fan-out resilience without Redis labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nMARATHON-4 Profiles: GET user and PATCH /api/users/me labels= ['architect', 'backend']\nMAR