g                 Set assignee\n      --depends-on stringArray          Add dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --description string              Set description\n      --description-from-file string    Read description from file (use - for stdin)\n      --design string                   Set design\n      --design-format string            Set design format (markdown or html)\n  -h, --help                            help for update\n      --notes string                    Set notes\n      --priority int                    Set priority\n      --remove-depends-on stringArray   Remove dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --remove-label stringArray        Remove label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --status string                   Set status\n      --title string                    Set title\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\nMARATHON-2.md\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process topology, port map, node identity, and local-only Redis.\n\n## Technical Approach\n","stderr":"","executionTime":102,"interleavedOutput":"Update issue fields\n\nUsage:\n  loom data update <issue-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --add-label stringArray           Add label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --assignee string                 Set assignee\n      --depends-on stringArray          Add dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --description string              Set description\n      --description-from-file string    Read description from file (use - for stdin)\n      --design string                   Set design\n      --design-format string            Set design format (markdown or html)\n  -h, --help                            help for update\n      --notes string                    Set notes\n      --priority int                    Set priority\n      --remove-depends-on stringArray   Remove dependency on issue ID (repeatable)\n      --remove-label stringArray        Remove label (repeatable); other labels are preserved\n      --status string                   Set status\n      --title string                    Set title\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n  -o, --output string       Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string       Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\nMARATHON-2.md\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process topology, port map, node identity, and local-only Redis.\n\n## Technical Approach\n","localExecutionTimeMs":40},"isBackground":false},"description":"Check loom update design CLI usage"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-b52aeb5c-08ad-44e7-9514-0cb9f9cb337d-24\nfc_6ea1d62c-bf52-91fb-9fb4-9ab62ed32330_0","startedAtMs":"1787427160729","completedAtMs":"1787427160832"},"model_call_id":"79777e32-7c2e-4792-93d8-906063980c15-9-fhsz","session_id":"5d026864-8168-490e-9120-8246ea733b1a","timestamp_ms":1787427160868}
