{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-3f5538e7-2dec-4f39-90d1-72c75771a783-19\nfc_61ecfffd-08d4-929a-ad0e-92cb4617393d_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-4 adds authenticated profile read and self-update on top of the MARATHON-3 `UserObj` / `users` table: `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a public profile (`200` / `404`), and `PATCH /api/users/me` mutates a validated subset of profile fields (`400` on bad timezone or over-length strings). Successful patches persist in the shared SQLite store (visible on every node) and emit a cluster-wide `user.updated` event through a no-op-safe broadcast hook that MARATHON-18 wires to WebSocket fan-out. This closes the gap between register-time profile defaults and live profile editing the SPA/settings flows need.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n- **Reuse MARATHON-3 identity stack:** Same `/app/data/huddle.db` `users` row, same `publicUser(row) → UserObj`, same `requireUser` / bearer middleware. No second user store.\n- **Routes live under `/api/users`:** New module `server/users/routes.js` (HTTP only). Persistence helpers (`findUserById`, `updateUserProfile`) extend `server/auth/users.js` so DDL ownership stays with auth.\n- **Mutable PATCH subset only:** `display_name`, `timezone`, `avatar_url`, `status_text`, `status_emoji`. **Never** allow `id`, `username`, password fields, or token mutation via this route.\n- **Timezone validation:** Accept only IANA time zone names. Prefer `Intl.supportedValuesOf('timeZone')` when available (Node 20+); otherwise validate by constructing `new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { timeZone })` and rejecting on throw. `\"UTC\"` remains valid. Do **not** invent offset-only strings like `\"UTC+1\"` as valid unless they appear in the IANA list.\n- **Length caps (authoritative):** enforce on the server with JS string `.length` (same length model as MARATHON-3 passwords).\n- **WS hook, not WS implementation:** After a successful DB commit, call `emitUserUpdated(userObj)` from `server/events/userUpdated.js`. Default export is a no-op (or in-process listener list). MARATHON-18 replaces/registers the real global WS broadcast. HTTP success **must not** depend on Redis or WS being up.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| Return bare `UserObj` without `{ \"user\": ... }` wrapper | Breaks symmetry with `GET /api/auth/me` and register/login envelopes fixed in MARATHON-3 |\n| Allow PATCH to rename `username` | Username is the durable login identity (case-insensitive unique); renaming needs a separate task and migration story |\n| Require workspace membership to GET a user | Workspaces are MARATHON-5; until then any authenticated user may resolve any `user.id` (global directory) |\n| Put profile columns in a separate `profiles` table | Unnecessary join; MARATHON-3 already defined columns on `users` |\n| Block PATCH until MARATHON-18 ships | Task explicitly says hook up when WS exists; profile REST must work without WS |\n| Soft-validate timezone (accept any string) | Task requires timezone validation → `400` |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nGlobal directory lookup (any authed user → any user id) is simpler than workspace-scoped visibility but leaks existence of all accounts by UUID. Acceptable for this marathon; MARATHON-5+ may tighten visibility later without changing `UserObj` shape.\n\n### Conventions inherited (authoritative)\n| Source | Convention |\n|--------|------------|\n| MARATHON-2 | `/app`, `server/index.js`, `/api/...`, JSON `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`, three nodes, `/app/data/` |\n| MARATHON-3 | `UserObj` seven fields; error `{ \"error\": string }`; bearer `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; SQLite `/app/data/huddle.db`; `requireUser`; ignore unknown JSON keys on write |\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared: `UserObj` (unchanged from MARATHON-3)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<uuid-string>\",\n  \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n  \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n  \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n  \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n}\n```\n\nAll seven keys always present in responses. Never include password, hash, salt, or token.\n\n### Patchable field limits (server-authoritative)\n\n| Field | Type | Max `.length` | Empty string | Notes |\n|-------|------|---------------|--------------|-------|\n| `display_name` | string | 64 | allowed | Trim leading/trailing whitespace before length check and store; empty after trim → store `\"\"` |\n| `timezone` | string | 64 (and IANA-valid) | **not** allowed | Must be non-empty IANA name (e.g. `UTC`, `America/New_York`) |\n| `avatar_url` | string | 2048 | allowed | No scheme check required; store as given after type check (do not trim interior spaces) |\n| `status_text` | string | 100 | allowed | Trim ends; empty → `\"\"` |\n| `status_emoji` | string | 32 | allowed | Trim ends; empty → `\"\"`; multi-codepoint emoji OK within length |\n\n**Partial update semantics:** Only keys **present** in the JSON object are updated. Omitted keys stay unchanged. Wrong type (`null`, number, object, array) for a present key → `400`. Empty object `{}` → `200` with unchanged `UserObj` (no WS emit if nothing changed).\n\n**Forbidden keys if present with any value:** `id`, `username`, `password`, `password_hash`, `password_salt`, `token` → `400` `{ \"error\": string }` (do not silently ignore identity/credential fields).\n\nOther unknown keys → ignore (same as MARATHON-3 register).\n\n---\n\n### C1 — `GET /api/users/{id}`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required (`requireUser`) |\n| Path param | `id` — opaque user UUID string (exact match to `users.id`) |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` |\n| Not found | `404` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Unauthenticated | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Wrong method | `405` or `404`; must not `500` |\n\n**Server:**\n1. Resolve bearer → user or `401`.\n2. If path is exactly `/api/users/me` on GET: treat `id` as the literal string `me` → **404** (self profile remains `GET /api/auth/me`). Do not special-case.\n3. Look up `users.id = id`; missing → `404`.\n4. Return `publicUser` envelope.\n\n**Who validates:** Server owns UUID existence. Client must not assume every id from messages still exists.\n\n**Client (SPA / MARATHON-21–23) while slow/failing:**\n- While pending: keep prior cached profile or show a neutral placeholder; do not flash logged-out.\n- On `200`: render `user.display_name` (fallback UX: `username` if display_name empty).\n- On `404`: show “user not found”; do not clear session.\n- On `401`: clear `huddle.token`, show login (same as `/api/auth/me`).\n- On network/5xx: show transient error; retry allowed.\n\n---\n\n### C2 — `PATCH /api/users/me`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required (`requireUser`) — updates **only** the authenticated user |\n| Body | JSON object; subset of patchable fields above |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` (post-update row) |\n| Validation failure | `400` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Unauthenticated | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Malformed JSON / non-object | `400` |\n\n**Server algorithm:**\n1. `requireUser` or `401`.\n2. `readJson` → must be a plain object.\n3. Validate each present key per table; collect updates.\n4. If any forbidden key present → `400` before writes.\n5. If updates non-empty: `UPDATE users SET ... WHERE id = ?` in SQLite; re-read row; `publicUser`.\n6. If at least one field actually changed: call `emitUserUpdated(userObj)` (best-effort; errors logged, HTTP still `200`).\n7. If no fields changed: return `200` with current user; **do not** emit.\n\n**Who validates:** Server is source of truth for IANA timezone and lengths. Client may pre-check for UX but must handle `400`.\n\n**Client while slow/failing:**\n- Disable save control / show pending on profile form until response.\n- Optimistic UI optional; on `400` revert fields and show `error` string.\n- On `200`: replace local current-user state with returned `user`; also expect eventual `user.updated` WS (when MARATHON-18 exists) and reconcile by `user.id`.\n- On `401`: logout flow.\n- On network/5xx: keep form dirty state; show retry; **MUST NOT** assume server applied the patch.\n\n---\n\n### C3 — `user.updated` broadcast seam (owned here; delivered by MARATHON-18)\n\n**Event name:** `user.updated`  \n**Scope:** Global — all authenticated WS connections on all nodes (when hub exists), not channel-scoped.  \n**Payload (WS frame / hub message body):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"user.updated\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n    \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n    \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n    \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n    \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n    \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Module contract:**\n\n```\n// server/events/userUpdated.js\nemitUserUpdated(user: UserObj): void\nregisterUserUpdatedListener(fn: (user: UserObj) => void): void  // optional helper for tests / WS hub\n```\n\n- MARATHON-4 always calls `emitUserUpdated` after a mutating PATCH.\n- Until MARATHON-18 registers a listener / Redis publish, emit is a no-op (in-process listeners only if registered).\n- MARATHON-18/19 own cross-node fan-out; this task does **not** publish to Redis directly (avoids inventing the pub/sub envelope twice). If implementer prefers a tiny in-process EventEmitter only, that is enough for C3.\n\n**Client when WS exists:** On `user.updated`, update any rendered profile/message author chrome for matching `user.id`. If WS is down, HTTP GET/PATCH remain correct; stale UI until refresh is acceptable.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema change\n**None required** if MARATHON-3 DDL already created:\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | Immutable via PATCH |\n| `username` / `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Immutable via PATCH |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Mutable |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | Mutable; IANA |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| password / salt / `created_at` | — | — | Untouched |\n\n**Backward compatibility:** Additive routes only. Existing auth responses keep working. No column drops/renames.\n\n**If MARATHON-3 columns are somehow missing** (partial implement): implementer adds the same `ALTER TABLE` / DDL defaults as MARATHON-3 — do not invent alternate names.\n\nNo new tables.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/users/routes.js` | Handlers: `GET /api/users/:id`, `PATCH /api/users/me`; path parse; status codes per C1/C2; call validation + store + `emitUserUpdated` |\n| `server/users/validate.js` | `assertPatchBody(obj) → { updates } \\| { error }` — length, type, IANA timezone, forbidden keys |\n| `server/events/userUpdated.js` | `emitUserUpdated`, optional `registerUserUpdatedListener`; default no-op fan-out |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/users.js` | Add `findUserById(id) → row \\| null`, `updateUserProfile(id, updates) → row` (UPDATE only provided columns); keep `publicUser` as single serializer |\n| `server/index.js` | After auth routes: dispatch `PATCH` `/api/users/me` and `GET` `/api/users/*` before generic 404; keep health + auth behavior unchanged |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Reuse `readJson` / `sendJson` if MARATHON-3 added them; otherwise use the same helpers auth routes use (do not duplicate divergent JSON error shapes) |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` / `redis.conf` / health | MARATHON-2 |\n| `server/auth/routes.js` register/login/me contracts | Unchanged; PATCH is not `/api/auth/me` |\n| SPA / static UI | MARATHON-21–23 |\n| WS router / Redis pubsub | MARATHON-18/19 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `findUserById` / `updateUserProfile` + validator  \n2. `userUpdated` event stub  \n3. HTTP routes + `index.js` wiring  \n4. Cross-node check: PATCH on :8000 → GET user on :8001  \n\n### Parallelism\n- Backend-only implementation.\n- Frontend settings UI (MARATHON-23) can be designed against C2; implement against live API after this lands.\n- MARATHON-18 can implement WS listen/subscribe in parallel using C3 payload; must call `registerUserUpdatedListener` or equivalent from the hub boot.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| C1 GET user by id | Messages/members UIs; mentions; SPA profile popovers |\n| C2 PATCH `/api/users/me` | SPA settings (MARATHON-23); any client editing status/timezone |\n| C3 `user.updated` payload + `emitUserUpdated` | MARATHON-18 WS global broadcast; MARATHON-19 fan-out must carry this event type when Redis is down |\n| Length/IANA rules | All writers of profile fields (no other writer should bypass validator) |\n\n### Build order vs siblings\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-3 (`users` table, `requireUser`, `publicUser`). MARATHON-2 for process topology.\n- **Soft-blocked on WS delivery:** none for HTTP acceptance; WS delivery blocked on MARATHON-18.\n- **Does not block:** workspace/channel CRUD can proceed; they should embed `UserObj` via `publicUser` when returning members.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Actual WS subscribe + global emit over Redis | MARATHON-18 / MARATHON-19 |\n| SPA profile/settings forms + testids | MARATHON-21 / MARATHON-23 |\n| Username change / password change APIs | New task if ever required |\n| Workspace-scoped profile visibility | Optional later under MARATHON-5+ |\n| Avatar file upload | MARATHON-11 (files); this task only stores URL string |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan (architect worktree = baseline `timer.sh` only; sibling `backend-dev-1` has MARATHON-2 `server/index.js`, `server/health.js`, `start.sh`, tests — **no** `/api/users` or auth modules yet; `/app` same baseline; grep for `UserObj` / `timezone` / `user.updated` / `/api/users` → no implementation hits):\n\n| Finding | Why excluded |\n|---------|----------------|\n| `server/health.js`, `GET /api/health`, `start.sh`, Redis | MARATHON-2 |\n| `POST /api/auth/*`, `GET /api/auth/me`, token/password DDL | MARATHON-3 (prerequisite; do not re-specify) |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\n| WS `/api/ws`, dense seq, resume | MARATHON-18 |\n| Redis-down fan-out | MARATHON-19 |\n| IRC nick/profile bridging | MARATHON-20 |\n| SPA auth + settings UI | MARATHON-21–23 |\n| File upload for avatars | MARATHON-11 |\n| Workspaces/members embedding users | MARATHON-5 |\n| Rate limiting profile writes | Not required |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| GET unknown UUID | `404` `{error}` |\n| GET valid id without auth | `401` |\n| GET `/api/users/me` | `404` (literal id `me`); use `/api/auth/me` |\n| PATCH without auth | `401` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"Not/AZone\"` | `400` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"\"` | `400` |\n| PATCH `display_name` length 65 | `400` |\n| PATCH `status_text` length 101 | `400` |\n| PATCH `status_emoji` length 33 | `400` |\n| PATCH `avatar_url` length 2049 | `400` |\n| PATCH includes `username` | `400` (forbidden key) |\n| PATCH includes only unknown keys | Treat as `{}` → `200`, no emit |\n| PATCH `display_name: \"  Alice  \"` | Store `\"Alice\"` (trimmed) |\n| PATCH `display_name: \"   \"` | Store `\"\"` |\n| PATCH `status_emoji: \"🚀\"` | `200` if `.length ≤ 32` |\n| Concurrent PATCH same user on two nodes | Last writer wins per field set; both may emit `user.updated`; acceptable |\n| SQLITE_BUSY | Respect `busy_timeout`; if still failing → `500` `{error}`; no partial HTTP success |\n| `emitUserUpdated` throws | Log stderr; still return `200` with saved user |\n| Redis down | PATCH/GET unaffected |\n| User deleted (future) while GET | N/A now (no delete API); if row missing → `404` |\n| Non-JSON PATCH body | `400` |\n| `Content-Type` missing but body is JSON | Best-effort parse; fail → `400` |\n| Method `PUT`/`POST` on `/api/users/me` | `405` or `404`; must not apply updates |\n| Extra whitespace in IANA zone `\" America/New_York\"` | `400` (do not auto-trim timezone; must match IANA exactly) |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated `GET /api/users/{id}` for an existing user → `200` `{user}` with all seven `UserObj` fields matching DB.\n2. Authenticated GET for unknown id → `404` with JSON `error`.\n3. GET without bearer (or bad token) → `401`.\n4. `PATCH /api/users/me` with valid `{ \"display_name\": \"Ada\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\" }` → `200`; subsequent `GET /api/auth/me` and `GET /api/users/{id}` on **another node** reflect updates.\n5. PATCH with invalid timezone → `400`; DB row unchanged.\n6. PATCH with over-length `status_text` / `display_name` / `avatar_url` / `status_emoji` → `400`; DB unchanged.\n7. PATCH body attempting `username` or `id` change → `400`; username unchanged.\n8. PATCH `{}` → `200`; user unchanged.\n9. After a mutating PATCH, `emitUserUpdated` is invoked with the new `UserObj` (verifiable via test listener); HTTP still `200` if no WS hub registered.\n10. **MUST NOT** include password/hash/salt/token in GET/PATCH responses.\n11. **MUST NOT** require Redis or WS for GET/PATCH success.\n12. **MUST NOT** change `GET /api/health` or auth register/login/me success contracts.\n13. Responses use `Content-Type: application/json` (charset utf-8 preferred).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Scripted (implementer / QA)\n```bash\n# cluster up; TOKEN from register on :8000; USER_ID from response\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/users/$USER_ID\n# expect 200\n\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/$(uuidgen)\n# expect 404\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"display_name\":\"Ada\",\"timezone\":\"America/New_York\",\"status_text\":\"ship it\",\"status_emoji\":\"🚀\"}'\n# expect 200\n\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/auth/me\n# expect updated fields\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"timezone\":\"Not/A_Real_Zone\"}'\n# expect 400\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"status_text\":\"'\"$(python3 -c 'print(\"x\"*101)\"')\"'\"}'\n# expect 400\n```\n\n### Scenarios that matter\n- Cross-node read-after-write for profile fields.\n- Forbidden username patch.\n- IANA reject vs `UTC` / `Europe/London` accept.\n- Emit hook called only when a field changes.\n- Redis killed: PATCH still `200`.\n\n### Manual human verification\nRegister a user, PATCH status/timezone, confirm GET on another port, confirm `/api/auth/me` matches. Optionally register a temporary listener in a REPL/unit test to assert `user.updated` payload shape.\n\n### Out of scope for this task’s tests\nSPA forms, actual WS client receipt, IRC, workspace member lists.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-3f5538e7-2dec-4f39-90d1-72c75771a783-19\nfc_61ecfffd-08d4-929a-ad0e-92cb4617393d_0","simpleCommands":["cat","wc"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"wc","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md"}],"fullText":"wc -c /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Write MARATHON-4 design to temp file","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"df2cb128-56ba-4615-93d5-837bf1f86c15","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"description":"Write MARATHON-4 design to temp file"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-3f5538e7-2dec-4f39-90d1-72c75771a783-19\nfc_61ecfffd-08d4-929a-ad0e-92cb4617393d_0","startedAtMs":"1787427503689"},"model_call_id":"77b7e082-c0d3-4b3d-8de4-5a432a4be929-8-eiyj","session_id":"df2cb128-56ba-4615-93d5-837bf1f86c15","timestamp_ms":1787427503733}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-3f5538e7-2dec-4f39-90d1-72c75771a783-19\nfc_61ecfffd-08d4-929a-ad0e-92cb4617393d_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-4 adds authenticated profile read and self-update on top of the MARATHON-3 `UserObj` / `users` table: `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a public profile (`200` / `404`), and `PATCH /api/users/me` mutates a validated subset of profile fields (`400` on bad timezone or over-length strings). Successful patches persist in the shared SQLite store (visible on every node) and emit a cluster-wide `user.updated` event through a no-op-safe broadcast hook that MARATHON-18 wires to WebSocket fan-out. This closes the gap between register-time profile defaults and live profile editing the SPA/settings flows need.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n- **Reuse MARATHON-3 identity stack:** Same `/app/data/huddle.db` `users` row, same `publicUser(row) → UserObj`, same `requireUser` / bearer middleware. No second user store.\n- **Routes live under `/api/users`:** New module `server/users/routes.js` (HTTP only). Persistence helpers (`findUserById`, `updateUserProfile`) extend `server/auth/users.js` so DDL ownership stays with auth.\n- **Mutable PATCH subset only:** `display_name`, `timezone`, `avatar_url`, `status_text`, `status_emoji`. **Never** allow `id`, `username`, password fields, or token mutation via this route.\n- **Timezone validation:** Accept only IANA time zone names. Prefer `Intl.supportedValuesOf('timeZone')` when available (Node 20+); otherwise validate by constructing `new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { timeZone })` and rejecting on throw. `\"UTC\"` remains valid. Do **not** invent offset-only strings like `\"UTC+1\"` as valid unless they appear in the IANA list.\n- **Length caps (authoritative):** enforce on the server with JS string `.length` (same length model as MARATHON-3 passwords).\n- **WS hook, not WS implementation:** After a successful DB commit, call `emitUserUpdated(userObj)` from `server/events/userUpdated.js`. Default export is a no-op (or in-process listener list). MARATHON-18 replaces/registers the real global WS broadcast. HTTP success **must not** depend on Redis or WS being up.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| Return bare `UserObj` without `{ \"user\": ... }` wrapper | Breaks symmetry with `GET /api/auth/me` and register/login envelopes fixed in MARATHON-3 |\n| Allow PATCH to rename `username` | Username is the durable login identity (case-insensitive unique); renaming needs a separate task and migration story |\n| Require workspace membership to GET a user | Workspaces are MARATHON-5; until then any authenticated user may resolve any `user.id` (global directory) |\n| Put profile columns in a separate `profiles` table | Unnecessary join; MARATHON-3 already defined columns on `users` |\n| Block PATCH until MARATHON-18 ships | Task explicitly says hook up when WS exists; profile REST must work without WS |\n| Soft-validate timezone (accept any string) | Task requires timezone validation → `400` |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nGlobal directory lookup (any authed user → any user id) is simpler than workspace-scoped visibility but leaks existence of all accounts by UUID. Acceptable for this marathon; MARATHON-5+ may tighten visibility later without changing `UserObj` shape.\n\n### Conventions inherited (authoritative)\n| Source | Convention |\n|--------|------------|\n| MARATHON-2 | `/app`, `server/index.js`, `/api/...`, JSON `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`, three nodes, `/app/data/` |\n| MARATHON-3 | `UserObj` seven fields; error `{ \"error\": string }`; bearer `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; SQLite `/app/data/huddle.db`; `requireUser`; ignore unknown JSON keys on write |\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared: `UserObj` (unchanged from MARATHON-3)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<uuid-string>\",\n  \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n  \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n  \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n  \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n}\n```\n\nAll seven keys always present in responses. Never include password, hash, salt, or token.\n\n### Patchable field limits (server-authoritative)\n\n| Field | Type | Max `.length` | Empty string | Notes |\n|-------|------|---------------|--------------|-------|\n| `display_name` | string | 64 | allowed | Trim leading/trailing whitespace before length check and store; empty after trim → store `\"\"` |\n| `timezone` | string | 64 (and IANA-valid) | **not** allowed | Must be non-empty IANA name (e.g. `UTC`, `America/New_York`) |\n| `avatar_url` | string | 2048 | allowed | No scheme check required; store as given after type check (do not trim interior spaces) |\n| `status_text` | string | 100 | allowed | Trim ends; empty → `\"\"` |\n| `status_emoji` | string | 32 | allowed | Trim ends; empty → `\"\"`; multi-codepoint emoji OK within length |\n\n**Partial update semantics:** Only keys **present** in the JSON object are updated. Omitted keys stay unchanged. Wrong type (`null`, number, object, array) for a present key → `400`. Empty object `{}` → `200` with unchanged `UserObj` (no WS emit if nothing changed).\n\n**Forbidden keys if present with any value:** `id`, `username`, `password`, `password_hash`, `password_salt`, `token` → `400` `{ \"error\": string }` (do not silently ignore identity/credential fields).\n\nOther unknown keys → ignore (same as MARATHON-3 register).\n\n---\n\n### C1 — `GET /api/users/{id}`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required (`requireUser`) |\n| Path param | `id` — opaque user UUID string (exact match to `users.id`) |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` |\n| Not found | `404` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Unauthenticated | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Wrong method | `405` or `404`; must not `500` |\n\n**Server:**\n1. Resolve bearer → user or `401`.\n2. If path is exactly `/api/users/me` on GET: treat `id` as the literal string `me` → **404** (self profile remains `GET /api/auth/me`). Do not special-case.\n3. Look up `users.id = id`; missing → `404`.\n4. Return `publicUser` envelope.\n\n**Who validates:** Server owns UUID existence. Client must not assume every id from messages still exists.\n\n**Client (SPA / MARATHON-21–23) while slow/failing:**\n- While pending: keep prior cached profile or show a neutral placeholder; do not flash logged-out.\n- On `200`: render `user.display_name` (fallback UX: `username` if display_name empty).\n- On `404`: show “user not found”; do not clear session.\n- On `401`: clear `huddle.token`, show login (same as `/api/auth/me`).\n- On network/5xx: show transient error; retry allowed.\n\n---\n\n### C2 — `PATCH /api/users/me`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required (`requireUser`) — updates **only** the authenticated user |\n| Body | JSON object; subset of patchable fields above |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` (post-update row) |\n| Validation failure | `400` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Unauthenticated | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Malformed JSON / non-object | `400` |\n\n**Server algorithm:**\n1. `requireUser` or `401`.\n2. `readJson` → must be a plain object.\n3. Validate each present key per table; collect updates.\n4. If any forbidden key present → `400` before writes.\n5. If updates non-empty: `UPDATE users SET ... WHERE id = ?` in SQLite; re-read row; `publicUser`.\n6. If at least one field actually changed: call `emitUserUpdated(userObj)` (best-effort; errors logged, HTTP still `200`).\n7. If no fields changed: return `200` with current user; **do not** emit.\n\n**Who validates:** Server is source of truth for IANA timezone and lengths. Client may pre-check for UX but must handle `400`.\n\n**Client while slow/failing:**\n- Disable save control / show pending on profile form until response.\n- Optimistic UI optional; on `400` revert fields and show `error` string.\n- On `200`: replace local current-user state with returned `user`; also expect eventual `user.updated` WS (when MARATHON-18 exists) and reconcile by `user.id`.\n- On `401`: logout flow.\n- On network/5xx: keep form dirty state; show retry; **MUST NOT** assume server applied the patch.\n\n---\n\n### C3 — `user.updated` broadcast seam (owned here; delivered by MARATHON-18)\n\n**Event name:** `user.updated`  \n**Scope:** Global — all authenticated WS connections on all nodes (when hub exists), not channel-scoped.  \n**Payload (WS frame / hub message body):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"user.updated\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n    \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n    \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n    \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n    \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n    \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Module contract:**\n\n```\n// server/events/userUpdated.js\nemitUserUpdated(user: UserObj): void\nregisterUserUpdatedListener(fn: (user: UserObj) => void): void  // optional helper for tests / WS hub\n```\n\n- MARATHON-4 always calls `emitUserUpdated` after a mutating PATCH.\n- Until MARATHON-18 registers a listener / Redis publish, emit is a no-op (in-process listeners only if registered).\n- MARATHON-18/19 own cross-node fan-out; this task does **not** publish to Redis directly (avoids inventing the pub/sub envelope twice). If implementer prefers a tiny in-process EventEmitter only, that is enough for C3.\n\n**Client when WS exists:** On `user.updated`, update any rendered profile/message author chrome for matching `user.id`. If WS is down, HTTP GET/PATCH remain correct; stale UI until refresh is acceptable.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema change\n**None required** if MARATHON-3 DDL already created:\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | Immutable via PATCH |\n| `username` / `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Immutable via PATCH |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Mutable |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | Mutable; IANA |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| password / salt / `created_at` | — | — | Untouched |\n\n**Backward compatibility:** Additive routes only. Existing auth responses keep working. No column drops/renames.\n\n**If MARATHON-3 columns are somehow missing** (partial implement): implementer adds the same `ALTER TABLE` / DDL defaults as MARATHON-3 — do not invent alternate names.\n\nNo new tables.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/users/routes.js` | Handlers: `GET /api/users/:id`, `PATCH /api/users/me`; path parse; status codes per C1/C2; call validation + store + `emitUserUpdated` |\n| `server/users/validate.js` | `assertPatchBody(obj) → { updates } \\| { error }` — length, type, IANA timezone, forbidden keys |\n| `server/events/userUpdated.js` | `emitUserUpdated`, optional `registerUserUpdatedListener`; default no-op fan-out |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/users.js` | Add `findUserById(id) → row \\| null`, `updateUserProfile(id, updates) → row` (UPDATE only provided columns); keep `publicUser` as single serializer |\n| `server/index.js` | After auth routes: dispatch `PATCH` `/api/users/me` and `GET` `/api/users/*` before generic 404; keep health + auth behavior unchanged |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Reuse `readJson` / `sendJson` if MARATHON-3 added them; otherwise use the same helpers auth routes use (do not duplicate divergent JSON error shapes) |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` / `redis.conf` / health | MARATHON-2 |\n| `server/auth/routes.js` register/login/me contracts | Unchanged; PATCH is not `/api/auth/me` |\n| SPA / static UI | MARATHON-21–23 |\n| WS router / Redis pubsub | MARATHON-18/19 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `findUserById` / `updateUserProfile` + validator  \n2. `userUpdated` event stub  \n3. HTTP routes + `index.js` wiring  \n4. Cross-node check: PATCH on :8000 → GET user on :8001  \n\n### Parallelism\n- Backend-only implementation.\n- Frontend settings UI (MARATHON-23) can be designed against C2; implement against live API after this lands.\n- MARATHON-18 can implement WS listen/subscribe in parallel using C3 payload; must call `registerUserUpdatedListener` or equivalent from the hub boot.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| C1 GET user by id | Messages/members UIs; mentions; SPA profile popovers |\n| C2 PATCH `/api/users/me` | SPA settings (MARATHON-23); any client editing status/timezone |\n| C3 `user.updated` payload + `emitUserUpdated` | MARATHON-18 WS global broadcast; MARATHON-19 fan-out must carry this event type when Redis is down |\n| Length/IANA rules | All writers of profile fields (no other writer should bypass validator) |\n\n### Build order vs siblings\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-3 (`users` table, `requireUser`, `publicUser`). MARATHON-2 for process topology.\n- **Soft-blocked on WS delivery:** none for HTTP acceptance; WS delivery blocked on MARATHON-18.\n- **Does not block:** workspace/channel CRUD can proceed; they should embed `UserObj` via `publicUser` when returning members.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Actual WS subscribe + global emit over Redis | MARATHON-18 / MARATHON-19 |\n| SPA profile/settings forms + testids | MARATHON-21 / MARATHON-23 |\n| Username change / password change APIs | New task if ever required |\n| Workspace-scoped profile visibility | Optional later under MARATHON-5+ |\n| Avatar file upload | MARATHON-11 (files); this task only stores URL string |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan (architect worktree = baseline `timer.sh` only; sibling `backend-dev-1` has MARATHON-2 `server/index.js`, `server/health.js`, `start.sh`, tests — **no** `/api/users` or auth modules yet; `/app` same baseline; grep for `UserObj` / `timezone` / `user.updated` / `/api/users` → no implementation hits):\n\n| Finding | Why excluded |\n|---------|----------------|\n| `server/health.js`, `GET /api/health`, `start.sh`, Redis | MARATHON-2 |\n| `POST /api/auth/*`, `GET /api/auth/me`, token/password DDL | MARATHON-3 (prerequisite; do not re-specify) |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\n| WS `/api/ws`, dense seq, resume | MARATHON-18 |\n| Redis-down fan-out | MARATHON-19 |\n| IRC nick/profile bridging | MARATHON-20 |\n| SPA auth + settings UI | MARATHON-21–23 |\n| File upload for avatars | MARATHON-11 |\n| Workspaces/members embedding users | MARATHON-5 |\n| Rate limiting profile writes | Not required |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| GET unknown UUID | `404` `{error}` |\n| GET valid id without auth | `401` |\n| GET `/api/users/me` | `404` (literal id `me`); use `/api/auth/me` |\n| PATCH without auth | `401` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"Not/AZone\"` | `400` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"\"` | `400` |\n| PATCH `display_name` length 65 | `400` |\n| PATCH `status_text` length 101 | `400` |\n| PATCH `status_emoji` length 33 | `400` |\n| PATCH `avatar_url` length 2049 | `400` |\n| PATCH includes `username` | `400` (forbidden key) |\n| PATCH includes only unknown keys | Treat as `{}` → `200`, no emit |\n| PATCH `display_name: \"  Alice  \"` | Store `\"Alice\"` (trimmed) |\n| PATCH `display_name: \"   \"` | Store `\"\"` |\n| PATCH `status_emoji: \"🚀\"` | `200` if `.length ≤ 32` |\n| Concurrent PATCH same user on two nodes | Last writer wins per field set; both may emit `user.updated`; acceptable |\n| SQLITE_BUSY | Respect `busy_timeout`; if still failing → `500` `{error}`; no partial HTTP success |\n| `emitUserUpdated` throws | Log stderr; still return `200` with saved user |\n| Redis down | PATCH/GET unaffected |\n| User deleted (future) while GET | N/A now (no delete API); if row missing → `404` |\n| Non-JSON PATCH body | `400` |\n| `Content-Type` missing but body is JSON | Best-effort parse; fail → `400` |\n| Method `PUT`/`POST` on `/api/users/me` | `405` or `404`; must not apply updates |\n| Extra whitespace in IANA zone `\" America/New_York\"` | `400` (do not auto-trim timezone; must match IANA exactly) |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated `GET /api/users/{id}` for an existing user → `200` `{user}` with all seven `UserObj` fields matching DB.\n2. Authenticated GET for unknown id → `404` with JSON `error`.\n3. GET without bearer (or bad token) → `401`.\n4. `PATCH /api/users/me` with valid `{ \"display_name\": \"Ada\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\" }` → `200`; subsequent `GET /api/auth/me` and `GET /api/users/{id}` on **another node** reflect updates.\n5. PATCH with invalid timezone → `400`; DB row unchanged.\n6. PATCH with over-length `status_text` / `display_name` / `avatar_url` / `status_emoji` → `400`; DB unchanged.\n7. PATCH body attempting `username` or `id` change → `400`; username unchanged.\n8. PATCH `{}` → `200`; user unchanged.\n9. After a mutating PATCH, `emitUserUpdated` is invoked with the new `UserObj` (verifiable via test listener); HTTP still `200` if no WS hub registered.\n10. **MUST NOT** include password/hash/salt/token in GET/PATCH responses.\n11. **MUST NOT** require Redis or WS for GET/PATCH success.\n12. **MUST NOT** change `GET /api/health` or auth register/login/me success contracts.\n13. Responses use `Content-Type: application/json` (charset utf-8 preferred).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Scripted (implementer / QA)\n```bash\n# cluster up; TOKEN from register on :8000; USER_ID from response\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/users/$USER_ID\n# expect 200\n\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/$(uuidgen)\n# expect 404\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"display_name\":\"Ada\",\"timezone\":\"America/New_York\",\"status_text\":\"ship it\",\"status_emoji\":\"🚀\"}'\n# expect 200\n\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/auth/me\n# expect updated fields\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"timezone\":\"Not/A_Real_Zone\"}'\n# expect 400\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"status_text\":\"'\"$(python3 -c 'print(\"x\"*101)\"')\"'\"}'\n# expect 400\n```\n\n### Scenarios that matter\n- Cross-node read-after-write for profile fields.\n- Forbidden username patch.\n- IANA reject vs `UTC` / `Europe/London` accept.\n- Emit hook called only when a field changes.\n- Redis killed: PATCH still `200`.\n\n### Manual human verification\nRegister a user, PATCH status/timezone, confirm GET on another port, confirm `/api/auth/me` matches. Optionally register a temporary listener in a REPL/unit test to assert `user.updated` payload shape.\n\n### Out of scope for this task’s tests\nSPA forms, actual WS client receipt, IRC, workspace member lists.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-3f5538e7-2dec-4f39-90d1-72c75771a783-19\nfc_61ecfffd-08d4-929a-ad0e-92cb4617393d_0","simpleCommands":["cat","wc"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cat","args":[],"fullText":"cat"},{"name":"wc","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"word","value":"/tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md"}],"fullText":"wc -c /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"cat"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Write MARATHON-4 design to temp file","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"df2cb128-56ba-4615-93d5-837bf1f86c15","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"cat > /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md << 'DESIGN_EOF'\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-4 adds authenticated profile read and self-update on top of the MARATHON-3 `UserObj` / `users` table: `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a public profile (`200` / `404`), and `PATCH /api/users/me` mutates a validated subset of profile fields (`400` on bad timezone or over-length strings). Successful patches persist in the shared SQLite store (visible on every node) and emit a cluster-wide `user.updated` event through a no-op-safe broadcast hook that MARATHON-18 wires to WebSocket fan-out. This closes the gap between register-time profile defaults and live profile editing the SPA/settings flows need.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n- **Reuse MARATHON-3 identity stack:** Same `/app/data/huddle.db` `users` row, same `publicUser(row) → UserObj`, same `requireUser` / bearer middleware. No second user store.\n- **Routes live under `/api/users`:** New module `server/users/routes.js` (HTTP only). Persistence helpers (`findUserById`, `updateUserProfile`) extend `server/auth/users.js` so DDL ownership stays with auth.\n- **Mutable PATCH subset only:** `display_name`, `timezone`, `avatar_url`, `status_text`, `status_emoji`. **Never** allow `id`, `username`, password fields, or token mutation via this route.\n- **Timezone validation:** Accept only IANA time zone names. Prefer `Intl.supportedValuesOf('timeZone')` when available (Node 20+); otherwise validate by constructing `new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { timeZone })` and rejecting on throw. `\"UTC\"` remains valid. Do **not** invent offset-only strings like `\"UTC+1\"` as valid unless they appear in the IANA list.\n- **Length caps (authoritative):** enforce on the server with JS string `.length` (same length model as MARATHON-3 passwords).\n- **WS hook, not WS implementation:** After a successful DB commit, call `emitUserUpdated(userObj)` from `server/events/userUpdated.js`. Default export is a no-op (or in-process listener list). MARATHON-18 replaces/registers the real global WS broadcast. HTTP success **must not** depend on Redis or WS being up.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| Return bare `UserObj` without `{ \"user\": ... }` wrapper | Breaks symmetry with `GET /api/auth/me` and register/login envelopes fixed in MARATHON-3 |\n| Allow PATCH to rename `username` | Username is the durable login identity (case-insensitive unique); renaming needs a separate task and migration story |\n| Require workspace membership to GET a user | Workspaces are MARATHON-5; until then any authenticated user may resolve any `user.id` (global directory) |\n| Put profile columns in a separate `profiles` table | Unnecessary join; MARATHON-3 already defined columns on `users` |\n| Block PATCH until MARATHON-18 ships | Task explicitly says hook up when WS exists; profile REST must work without WS |\n| Soft-validate timezone (accept any string) | Task requires timezone validation → `400` |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nGlobal directory lookup (any authed user → any user id) is simpler than workspace-scoped visibility but leaks existence of all accounts by UUID. Acceptable for this marathon; MARATHON-5+ may tighten visibility later without changing `UserObj` shape.\n\n### Conventions inherited (authoritative)\n| Source | Convention |\n|--------|------------|\n| MARATHON-2 | `/app`, `server/index.js`, `/api/...`, JSON `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`, three nodes, `/app/data/` |\n| MARATHON-3 | `UserObj` seven fields; error `{ \"error\": string }`; bearer `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; SQLite `/app/data/huddle.db`; `requireUser`; ignore unknown JSON keys on write |\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared: `UserObj` (unchanged from MARATHON-3)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<uuid-string>\",\n  \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n  \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n  \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n  \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n}\n```\n\nAll seven keys always present in responses. Never include password, hash, salt, or token.\n\n### Patchable field limits (server-authoritative)\n\n| Field | Type | Max `.length` | Empty string | Notes |\n|-------|------|---------------|--------------|-------|\n| `display_name` | string | 64 | allowed | Trim leading/trailing whitespace before length check and store; empty after trim → store `\"\"` |\n| `timezone` | string | 64 (and IANA-valid) | **not** allowed | Must be non-empty IANA name (e.g. `UTC`, `America/New_York`) |\n| `avatar_url` | string | 2048 | allowed | No scheme check required; store as given after type check (do not trim interior spaces) |\n| `status_text` | string | 100 | allowed | Trim ends; empty → `\"\"` |\n| `status_emoji` | string | 32 | allowed | Trim ends; empty → `\"\"`; multi-codepoint emoji OK within length |\n\n**Partial update semantics:** Only keys **present** in the JSON object are updated. Omitted keys stay unchanged. Wrong type (`null`, number, object, array) for a present key → `400`. Empty object `{}` → `200` with unchanged `UserObj` (no WS emit if nothing changed).\n\n**Forbidden keys if present with any value:** `id`, `username`, `password`, `password_hash`, `password_salt`, `token` → `400` `{ \"error\": string }` (do not silently ignore identity/credential fields).\n\nOther unknown keys → ignore (same as MARATHON-3 register).\n\n---\n\n### C1 — `GET /api/users/{id}`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required (`requireUser`) |\n| Path param | `id` — opaque user UUID string (exact match to `users.id`) |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` |\n| Not found | `404` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Unauthenticated | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Wrong method | `405` or `404`; must not `500` |\n\n**Server:**\n1. Resolve bearer → user or `401`.\n2. If path is exactly `/api/users/me` on GET: treat `id` as the literal string `me` → **404** (self profile remains `GET /api/auth/me`). Do not special-case.\n3. Look up `users.id = id`; missing → `404`.\n4. Return `publicUser` envelope.\n\n**Who validates:** Server owns UUID existence. Client must not assume every id from messages still exists.\n\n**Client (SPA / MARATHON-21–23) while slow/failing:**\n- While pending: keep prior cached profile or show a neutral placeholder; do not flash logged-out.\n- On `200`: render `user.display_name` (fallback UX: `username` if display_name empty).\n- On `404`: show “user not found”; do not clear session.\n- On `401`: clear `huddle.token`, show login (same as `/api/auth/me`).\n- On network/5xx: show transient error; retry allowed.\n\n---\n\n### C2 — `PATCH /api/users/me`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required (`requireUser`) — updates **only** the authenticated user |\n| Body | JSON object; subset of patchable fields above |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` (post-update row) |\n| Validation failure | `400` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Unauthenticated | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Malformed JSON / non-object | `400` |\n\n**Server algorithm:**\n1. `requireUser` or `401`.\n2. `readJson` → must be a plain object.\n3. Validate each present key per table; collect updates.\n4. If any forbidden key present → `400` before writes.\n5. If updates non-empty: `UPDATE users SET ... WHERE id = ?` in SQLite; re-read row; `publicUser`.\n6. If at least one field actually changed: call `emitUserUpdated(userObj)` (best-effort; errors logged, HTTP still `200`).\n7. If no fields changed: return `200` with current user; **do not** emit.\n\n**Who validates:** Server is source of truth for IANA timezone and lengths. Client may pre-check for UX but must handle `400`.\n\n**Client while slow/failing:**\n- Disable save control / show pending on profile form until response.\n- Optimistic UI optional; on `400` revert fields and show `error` string.\n- On `200`: replace local current-user state with returned `user`; also expect eventual `user.updated` WS (when MARATHON-18 exists) and reconcile by `user.id`.\n- On `401`: logout flow.\n- On network/5xx: keep form dirty state; show retry; **MUST NOT** assume server applied the patch.\n\n---\n\n### C3 — `user.updated` broadcast seam (owned here; delivered by MARATHON-18)\n\n**Event name:** `user.updated`  \n**Scope:** Global — all authenticated WS connections on all nodes (when hub exists), not channel-scoped.  \n**Payload (WS frame / hub message body):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"user.updated\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n    \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n    \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n    \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n    \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n    \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Module contract:**\n\n```\n// server/events/userUpdated.js\nemitUserUpdated(user: UserObj): void\nregisterUserUpdatedListener(fn: (user: UserObj) => void): void  // optional helper for tests / WS hub\n```\n\n- MARATHON-4 always calls `emitUserUpdated` after a mutating PATCH.\n- Until MARATHON-18 registers a listener / Redis publish, emit is a no-op (in-process listeners only if registered).\n- MARATHON-18/19 own cross-node fan-out; this task does **not** publish to Redis directly (avoids inventing the pub/sub envelope twice). If implementer prefers a tiny in-process EventEmitter only, that is enough for C3.\n\n**Client when WS exists:** On `user.updated`, update any rendered profile/message author chrome for matching `user.id`. If WS is down, HTTP GET/PATCH remain correct; stale UI until refresh is acceptable.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema change\n**None required** if MARATHON-3 DDL already created:\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | Immutable via PATCH |\n| `username` / `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Immutable via PATCH |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Mutable |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | Mutable; IANA |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| password / salt / `created_at` | — | — | Untouched |\n\n**Backward compatibility:** Additive routes only. Existing auth responses keep working. No column drops/renames.\n\n**If MARATHON-3 columns are somehow missing** (partial implement): implementer adds the same `ALTER TABLE` / DDL defaults as MARATHON-3 — do not invent alternate names.\n\nNo new tables.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/users/routes.js` | Handlers: `GET /api/users/:id`, `PATCH /api/users/me`; path parse; status codes per C1/C2; call validation + store + `emitUserUpdated` |\n| `server/users/validate.js` | `assertPatchBody(obj) → { updates } \\| { error }` — length, type, IANA timezone, forbidden keys |\n| `server/events/userUpdated.js` | `emitUserUpdated`, optional `registerUserUpdatedListener`; default no-op fan-out |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/users.js` | Add `findUserById(id) → row \\| null`, `updateUserProfile(id, updates) → row` (UPDATE only provided columns); keep `publicUser` as single serializer |\n| `server/index.js` | After auth routes: dispatch `PATCH` `/api/users/me` and `GET` `/api/users/*` before generic 404; keep health + auth behavior unchanged |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Reuse `readJson` / `sendJson` if MARATHON-3 added them; otherwise use the same helpers auth routes use (do not duplicate divergent JSON error shapes) |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` / `redis.conf` / health | MARATHON-2 |\n| `server/auth/routes.js` register/login/me contracts | Unchanged; PATCH is not `/api/auth/me` |\n| SPA / static UI | MARATHON-21–23 |\n| WS router / Redis pubsub | MARATHON-18/19 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `findUserById` / `updateUserProfile` + validator  \n2. `userUpdated` event stub  \n3. HTTP routes + `index.js` wiring  \n4. Cross-node check: PATCH on :8000 → GET user on :8001  \n\n### Parallelism\n- Backend-only implementation.\n- Frontend settings UI (MARATHON-23) can be designed against C2; implement against live API after this lands.\n- MARATHON-18 can implement WS listen/subscribe in parallel using C3 payload; must call `registerUserUpdatedListener` or equivalent from the hub boot.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| C1 GET user by id | Messages/members UIs; mentions; SPA profile popovers |\n| C2 PATCH `/api/users/me` | SPA settings (MARATHON-23); any client editing status/timezone |\n| C3 `user.updated` payload + `emitUserUpdated` | MARATHON-18 WS global broadcast; MARATHON-19 fan-out must carry this event type when Redis is down |\n| Length/IANA rules | All writers of profile fields (no other writer should bypass validator) |\n\n### Build order vs siblings\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-3 (`users` table, `requireUser`, `publicUser`). MARATHON-2 for process topology.\n- **Soft-blocked on WS delivery:** none for HTTP acceptance; WS delivery blocked on MARATHON-18.\n- **Does not block:** workspace/channel CRUD can proceed; they should embed `UserObj` via `publicUser` when returning members.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Actual WS subscribe + global emit over Redis | MARATHON-18 / MARATHON-19 |\n| SPA profile/settings forms + testids | MARATHON-21 / MARATHON-23 |\n| Username change / password change APIs | New task if ever required |\n| Workspace-scoped profile visibility | Optional later under MARATHON-5+ |\n| Avatar file upload | MARATHON-11 (files); this task only stores URL string |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan (architect worktree = baseline `timer.sh` only; sibling `backend-dev-1` has MARATHON-2 `server/index.js`, `server/health.js`, `start.sh`, tests — **no** `/api/users` or auth modules yet; `/app` same baseline; grep for `UserObj` / `timezone` / `user.updated` / `/api/users` → no implementation hits):\n\n| Finding | Why excluded |\n|---------|----------------|\n| `server/health.js`, `GET /api/health`, `start.sh`, Redis | MARATHON-2 |\n| `POST /api/auth/*`, `GET /api/auth/me`, token/password DDL | MARATHON-3 (prerequisite; do not re-specify) |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\n| WS `/api/ws`, dense seq, resume | MARATHON-18 |\n| Redis-down fan-out | MARATHON-19 |\n| IRC nick/profile bridging | MARATHON-20 |\n| SPA auth + settings UI | MARATHON-21–23 |\n| File upload for avatars | MARATHON-11 |\n| Workspaces/members embedding users | MARATHON-5 |\n| Rate limiting profile writes | Not required |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| GET unknown UUID | `404` `{error}` |\n| GET valid id without auth | `401` |\n| GET `/api/users/me` | `404` (literal id `me`); use `/api/auth/me` |\n| PATCH without auth | `401` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"Not/AZone\"` | `400` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"\"` | `400` |\n| PATCH `display_name` length 65 | `400` |\n| PATCH `status_text` length 101 | `400` |\n| PATCH `status_emoji` length 33 | `400` |\n| PATCH `avatar_url` length 2049 | `400` |\n| PATCH includes `username` | `400` (forbidden key) |\n| PATCH includes only unknown keys | Treat as `{}` → `200`, no emit |\n| PATCH `display_name: \"  Alice  \"` | Store `\"Alice\"` (trimmed) |\n| PATCH `display_name: \"   \"` | Store `\"\"` |\n| PATCH `status_emoji: \"🚀\"` | `200` if `.length ≤ 32` |\n| Concurrent PATCH same user on two nodes | Last writer wins per field set; both may emit `user.updated`; acceptable |\n| SQLITE_BUSY | Respect `busy_timeout`; if still failing → `500` `{error}`; no partial HTTP success |\n| `emitUserUpdated` throws | Log stderr; still return `200` with saved user |\n| Redis down | PATCH/GET unaffected |\n| User deleted (future) while GET | N/A now (no delete API); if row missing → `404` |\n| Non-JSON PATCH body | `400` |\n| `Content-Type` missing but body is JSON | Best-effort parse; fail → `400` |\n| Method `PUT`/`POST` on `/api/users/me` | `405` or `404`; must not apply updates |\n| Extra whitespace in IANA zone `\" America/New_York\"` | `400` (do not auto-trim timezone; must match IANA exactly) |\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Authenticated `GET /api/users/{id}` for an existing user → `200` `{user}` with all seven `UserObj` fields matching DB.\n2. Authenticated GET for unknown id → `404` with JSON `error`.\n3. GET without bearer (or bad token) → `401`.\n4. `PATCH /api/users/me` with valid `{ \"display_name\": \"Ada\", \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\" }` → `200`; subsequent `GET /api/auth/me` and `GET /api/users/{id}` on **another node** reflect updates.\n5. PATCH with invalid timezone → `400`; DB row unchanged.\n6. PATCH with over-length `status_text` / `display_name` / `avatar_url` / `status_emoji` → `400`; DB unchanged.\n7. PATCH body attempting `username` or `id` change → `400`; username unchanged.\n8. PATCH `{}` → `200`; user unchanged.\n9. After a mutating PATCH, `emitUserUpdated` is invoked with the new `UserObj` (verifiable via test listener); HTTP still `200` if no WS hub registered.\n10. **MUST NOT** include password/hash/salt/token in GET/PATCH responses.\n11. **MUST NOT** require Redis or WS for GET/PATCH success.\n12. **MUST NOT** change `GET /api/health` or auth register/login/me success contracts.\n13. Responses use `Content-Type: application/json` (charset utf-8 preferred).\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Scripted (implementer / QA)\n```bash\n# cluster up; TOKEN from register on :8000; USER_ID from response\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/users/$USER_ID\n# expect 200\n\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" \\\n  http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/$(uuidgen)\n# expect 404\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"display_name\":\"Ada\",\"timezone\":\"America/New_York\",\"status_text\":\"ship it\",\"status_emoji\":\"🚀\"}'\n# expect 200\n\ncurl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:8002/api/auth/me\n# expect updated fields\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"timezone\":\"Not/A_Real_Zone\"}'\n# expect 400\n\ncurl -sS -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/users/me \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"status_text\":\"'\"$(python3 -c 'print(\"x\"*101)\"')\"'\"}'\n# expect 400\n```\n\n### Scenarios that matter\n- Cross-node read-after-write for profile fields.\n- Forbidden username patch.\n- IANA reject vs `UTC` / `Europe/London` accept.\n- Emit hook called only when a field changes.\n- Redis killed: PATCH still `200`.\n\n### Manual human verification\nRegister a user, PATCH status/timezone, confirm GET on another port, confirm `/api/auth/me` matches. Optionally register a temporary listener in a REPL/unit test to assert `user.updated` payload shape.\n\n### Out of scope for this task’s tests\nSPA forms, actual WS client receipt, IRC, workspace member lists.\nDESIGN_EOF\nwc -c /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"18787 /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md\n","stderr":"","executionTime":116,"interleavedOutput":"18787 /tmp/MARATHON-4-design.md\n","localExecutionTimeMs":28},"isBackground":false},"description":"Write MARATHON-4 design to temp file"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-3f5538e7-2dec-4f39-90d1-72c75771a783-19\nfc_61ecfffd-08d4-929a-ad0e-92cb4617393d_0","startedAtMs":"1787427503689","completedAtMs":"1787427503808"},"model_call_id":"77b7e082-c0d3-4b3d-8de4-5a432a4be929-8-eiyj","session_id":"df2cb128-56ba-4615-93d5-837bf1f86c15","timestamp_ms":1787427503849}
