≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process t\n==== MARATHON-3 ====\ntitle: Auth: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nstatus: closed\nlabels: ['backend']\nnotes: Addressed FEEDBACK attempt=1: rebased auth onto MARATHON-2 head so start.sh, redis.conf, and bootstrap tests remain; DDL in server/db.js; register/login/me + cross-node SQLite verified; Redis-down auth verified.\ndesign_len: 19392\nhas_design: True\ndesign_preview: ## Summary\n\nMARATHON-3 implements cluster-wide authentication for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, plus the shared durable user/token store that all three HTTP nodes read and write. It establishes the `UserObj` identity shape, opaque bearer tokens (`Authorization: Bearer …`), password hashing, username slug validation, and a reusable auth middleware that every later authenticated route (workspaces, channels, WS, IRC `PASS`, SPA) will call. Withou\n==== MARATHON-4 ====\ntitle: Profiles: GET user and PATCH /api/users/me\nstatus: blocked\nlabels: ['backend']\nnotes: BLOCKED: Depends on MARATHON-3 (users table, requireUser, publicUser, auth middleware). MARATHON-3 is still in_progress and has not landed on main/harness-integrated head; this worktree only has MARATHON-2 bootstrap (no server/auth). Re-claim after MARATHON-3 merges.\ndesign_len: 18680\nhas_design: True\ndesign_preview: ## Summary\n\nMARATHON-4 adds authenticated profile read and self-update on top of the MARATHON-3 `UserObj` / `users` table: `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a public profile (`200` / `404`), and `PATCH /api/users/me` mutates a validated subset of profile fields (`400` on bad timezone or over-length strings). Successful patches persist in the shared SQLite store (visible on every node) and emit a cluster-wide `user.updated` event through a no-op-safe broadcast hook that MARATHON-18 wires to WebSocket\n==== MARATHON-5 ====\ntitle: Workspaces: create, list, detail, members, roles, ownership\nstatus: open\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\nnotes: \ndesign_len: 0\nhas_design: False\ndesign_preview: \n==== MARATHON-21 ====\ntitle: SPA shell: auth UI, token storage, logout/login\nstatus: in_progress\nlabels: ['architect', 'frontend']\nnotes: \ndesign_len: 0\nhas_design: False\ndesign_preview: \n==== MARATHON-22 ====\ntitle: SPA: workspaces, channels, three-pane layout, messages\nstatus: open\nlabels: ['architect', 'frontend']\nnotes: \ndesign_len: 0\nhas_design: False\ndesign_preview: \n","stderr":"time=2026-08-22T19:51:30.964Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:30.981Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:30.997Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:31.013Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:31.029Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:31.043Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\n","executionTime":146,"interleavedOutput":"==== MARATHON-2 ====\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:30.964Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntitle: Bootstrap cluster: start.sh, 3 HTTP nodes, Redis, health\nstatus: closed\nlabels: ['backend']\nnotes: Implemented start.sh supervisor (Redis :6379 + nodes :8000/8001/8002 with ~1s respawn), server/index.js + health.js (GET /api/health → {status:ok, node_id} number, Redis-independent), package.json, redis.conf. Verified: unit tests, integration (health map, node SIGKILL respawn ≤60s, Redis SIGKILL with health still 200). No migration.\ndesign_len: 14016\nhas_design: True\ndesign_preview: ## Summary\n\nMARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process t\n==== MARATHON-3 ====\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:30.981Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntitle: Auth: register, login, me, bearer tokens\nstatus: closed\nlabels: ['backend']\nnotes: Addressed FEEDBACK attempt=1: rebased auth onto MARATHON-2 head so start.sh, redis.conf, and bootstrap tests remain; DDL in server/db.js; register/login/me + cross-node SQLite verified; Redis-down auth verified.\ndesign_len: 19392\nhas_design: True\ndesign_preview: ## Summary\n\nMARATHON-3 implements cluster-wide authentication for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, plus the shared durable user/token store that all three HTTP nodes read and write. It establishes the `UserObj` identity shape, opaque bearer tokens (`Authorization: Bearer …`), password hashing, username slug validation, and a reusable auth middleware that every later authenticated route (workspaces, channels, WS, IRC `PASS`, SPA) will call. Withou\n==== MARATHON-4 ====\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:30.997Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntitle: Profiles: GET user and PATCH /api/users/me\nstatus: blocked\nlabels: ['backend']\nnotes: BLOCKED: Depends on MARATHON-3 (users table, requireUser, publicUser, auth middleware). MARATHON-3 is still in_progress and has not landed on main/harness-integrated head; this worktree only has MARATHON-2 bootstrap (no server/auth). Re-claim after MARATHON-3 merges.\ndesign_len: 18680\nhas_design: True\ndesign_preview: ## Summary\n\nMARATHON-4 adds authenticated profile read and self-update on top of the MARATHON-3 `UserObj` / `users` table: `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a public profile (`200` / `404`), and `PATCH /api/users/me` mutates a validated subset of profile fields (`400` on bad timezone or over-length strings). Successful patches persist in the shared SQLite store (visible on every node) and emit a cluster-wide `user.updated` event through a no-op-safe broadcast hook that MARATHON-18 wires to WebSocket\n==== MARATHON-5 ====\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:31.013Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntitle: Workspaces: create, list, detail, members, roles, ownership\nstatus: open\nlabels: ['architect', 'backend']\nnotes: \ndesign_len: 0\nhas_design: False\ndesign_preview: \n==== MARATHON-21 ====\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:31.029Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntitle: SPA shell: auth UI, token storage, logout/login\nstatus: in_progress\nlabels: ['architect', 'frontend']\nnotes: \ndesign_len: 0\nhas_design: False\ndesign_preview: \n==== MARATHON-22 ====\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:31.043Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntitle: SPA: workspaces, channels, three-pane layout, messages\nstatus: open\nlabels: ['architect', 'frontend']\nnotes: \ndesign_len: 0\nhas_design: False\ndesign_preview: \n","localExecutionTimeMs":106},"isBackground":false},"description":"Show notes/designs for key tasks"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-5b04dc50-006f-4320-8370-bcb6293e4e9f-6\nfc_ddbf69c1-b7b7-9d50-8111-660ecbd494da_1","startedAtMs":"1787428290924","completedAtMs":"1787428291070"},"model_call_id":"4dabf0fb-8eb4-4dfb-98f3-2bbb507fe57f-2-bgte","session_id":"0b561b47-2d17-430d-9c8e-044dfd49fd95