{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-145d4db2-5737-4991-9181-030aa62bb3af-12\nfc_c1dfcd3d-f597-9174-b2c0-ae8e9bd5b6ae_2","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"SPA|localStorage|huddle\\.token|auth-form|frontend|GET /|static|UserObj|Bearer","path":"/tmp/marathon-3-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-145d4db2-5737-4991-9181-030aa62bb3af-12\nfc_c1dfcd3d-f597-9174-b2c0-ae8e9bd5b6ae_2","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"SPA|localStorage|huddle\\.token|auth-form|frontend|GET /|static|UserObj|Bearer","path":"/tmp/marathon-3-design.md","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../tmp/marathon-3-design.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":3,"content":"MARATHON-3 implements cluster-wide authentication for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, plus the shared durable user/token store that all three HTTP nodes read and write. It establishes the `UserObj` identity shape, opaque bearer tokens (`Authorization: Bearer …`), password hashing, username slug validation, and a reusable auth middleware that every later authenticated route (workspaces, channels, WS, IRC `PASS`, SPA) will call. Without this seam, no other feature can attribute callers or survive a request to a different node.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":41,"content":"| `UserObj` public fields | `{id, username, display_name, timezone, avatar_url, status_text, status_emoji}` — always present on auth responses |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":45,"content":"| Bearer | Header `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (single space); token string length ≥ 16 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":51,"content":"### Shared: `UserObj` (public; never include password/hash/salt/token)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":85,"content":"| Success | `201` `{ \"user\": UserObj, \"token\": string }` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":98,"content":"**Client (SPA / MARATHON-21) while slow/failing:**","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":100,"content":"- On `201`: store `token` in `localStorage` key `huddle.token`; treat as logged-in; may call `GET /api/auth/me` or use returned `user`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":115,"content":"| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj, \"token\": string }` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":123,"content":"4. Issue new token; return `200` with full `UserObj` (current profile fields from DB).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":129,"content":"### C3 — `GET /api/auth/me`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":133,"content":"| Auth | Required: `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":135,"content":"| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":139,"content":"- Require header matching `/^Bearer\\s+(\\S+)$/i` (trim); extract token.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":141,"content":"- Do not accept token via query string on this route (query `?token=` is SPA/WS concern later).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":143,"content":"**Client:** On app load, if `huddle.token` set, call `/api/auth/me`; on `401` clear token and show login; while pending, may show a loading shell without claiming a user.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":149,"content":"A user registered or token issued on any of `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` must be accepted by the other two within normal SQLite visibility (immediately after the successful response returns). QA will register on one port and `GET /api/auth/me` on another with the same token.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":156,"content":"resolveBearerUser(authorizationHeader: string | null) → UserObj | null","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":157,"content":"requireUser(req, res) → UserObj | writes 401 and returns null","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":161,"content":"- Output: public `UserObj` only.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":205,"content":"| `server/auth/users.js` | `createUser(...)`, `findUserByUsername(username)`, `publicUser(row) → UserObj` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":206,"content":"| `server/auth/middleware.js` | `resolveBearerUser`, `requireUser` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":213,"content":"| `server/index.js` | Route `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me` before generic 404; keep `GET /api/health` behavior unchanged; initialize DB once at process start (fail boot if DB cannot open) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":221,"content":"| SPA / static HTML | MARATHON-21 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":234,"content":"- Frontend MARATHON-21 **architecture** can proceed from contracts C1–C3; **implementation** of SPA auth UI should land after (or against mocked) these endpoints.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":235,"content":"- MARATHON-4 (profiles) extends `users` columns usage and adds routes; must reuse `UserObj` + `requireUser`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":241,"content":"| C1/C2/C3 HTTP auth | MARATHON-21 SPA; QA grader |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":242,"content":"| `UserObj` shape | MARATHON-4, channel members, messages `author`, WS `user.updated` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":243,"content":"| Session table / `resolveBearerUser` | MARATHON-5…20 authenticated APIs; WS `?token=`; IRC `PASS` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":254,"content":"| Logout / token revoke endpoint | Not in API contract — SPA clears `huddle.token` only; optional later if needed |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":265,"content":"| `GET /api/health` / `start.sh` / Redis | MARATHON-2 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":266,"content":"| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":268,"content":"| SPA auth form, `huddle.token`, testids | MARATHON-21 (consumes C1–C3 only) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":292,"content":"| `Authorization: bearer <token>` | Accept case-insensitive `Bearer` scheme |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":293,"content":"| `Authorization: Bearer` with no token | `401` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":294,"content":"| Method wrong (e.g. `GET /api/auth/register`) | `405` or `404`; must not `500` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":305,"content":"1. `POST /api/auth/register` with valid `{username,password}` → `201`, body has `user` and `token`, `token.length >= 16`, `user` includes all seven `UserObj` fields.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":312,"content":"8. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` → `200` `{user}` matching the registered user id/username.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":314,"content":"10. Register on `127.0.0.1:8000`, then `GET /api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` with the same token → `200` (shared durable store).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":317,"content":"13. **MUST NOT:** change `GET /api/health` semantics or port/`node_id` mapping.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":329,"content":"curl -sS -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/auth/me","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":347,"content":"SPA form, logout UI, profile PATCH, workspace creation, WS/IRC token use.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":41,"totalMatchedLines":41,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-145d4db2-5737-4991-9181-030aa62bb3af-12\nfc_c1dfcd3d-f597-9174-b2c0-ae8e9bd5b6ae_2","startedAtMs":"1787428298536","completedAtMs":"1787428298980"},"model_call_id":"4dabf0fb-8eb4-4dfb-98f3-2bbb507fe57f-3-1bta","session_id":"0b561b47-2d17-430d-9c8e-044dfd49fd95","timestamp_ms":1787428299003}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-145d4db2-5737-4991-9181-030aa62bb3af-13\nfc_c1dfcd3d-f597-9174-b2c0-ae8e9bd5b6ae_3","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"SPA|static|GET /|html|frontend|serve","path":"/tmp/marathon-2-design.md","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-145d4db2-5737-4991-9181-030aa62bb3af-13\nfc_c1dfcd3d-f597-9174-b2c0-ae8e9bd5b6ae_3","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"SPA|static|GET /|html|frontend|serve","path":"/tmp/marathon-2-design.md","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/work/ws/worktrees/app/app-architect-1":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"../../../../../tmp/marathon-2-design.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":3,"content":"MARATHON-2 bootstraps the Huddle cluster runtime at `/app`: a foreground `start.sh` that launches local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, keeps them alive under SIGKILL (HTTP respawn ≤60s; Redis respawn after kill), and exposes a stable `GET /api/health` contract returning `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` with `node_id` ∈ `{0,1,2}` matching ports. This is the foundation every later auth, messaging, WS, IRC, and SPA task assumes: process topology, port map, node identity, and local-only Redis.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":8,"content":"- **Process model:** One bash supervisor (`/app/start.sh`) stays in the foreground and owns child lifetimes. Children: one `redis-server` + three Node.js HTTP workers. The supervisor polls PIDs (≈1s cadence) and respawns any dead child without exiting.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":10,"content":"- **Redis:** System `redis-server` (v7 present), bound to `127.0.0.1:6379`, persistence directory under `/app/data/redis`. Started as a non-daemon child of `start.sh` (no `--daemonize yes`) so the supervisor can track its PID.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":17,"content":"| Python HTTP (stdlib) | Viable, but SPA + WS + IRC gateway later fit one Node process better; env has no FastAPI/Flask |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":31,"content":"| HTTP runtime | Node.js, CommonJS or ESM; entry `server/index.js` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":41,"content":"### C1 — `GET /api/health` (each HTTP node)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":45,"content":"| Method / path | `GET /api/health` |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":56,"content":"**Owner:** Backend (this task). **Consumer:** QA harness, future load balancer checks, SPA may optionally display node identity later.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":79,"content":"No browser UI in this task. The only cross-seam contract is **C1**, which the SPA (MARATHON-21+) may call later from same-origin `fetch('/api/health')`. Until then, consumers are curl/QA. Unknown paths may return `404` with a small JSON error or plain 404—not part of acceptance beyond not crashing.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":91,"content":"| `REDIS_HOST` | string | optional, default `127.0.0.1` | Reserved for later tasks; unused by health |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":92,"content":"| `REDIS_PORT` | integer | optional, default `6379` | Reserved for later tasks |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":99,"content":"| `/app/data/` | Parent for future durable store (MARATHON-3+) | Reserved; no files required by this task |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":109,"content":"| `/app/server/index.js` | HTTP server entry: read `NODE_ID`/`PORT`, bind `127.0.0.1:$PORT`, route `GET /api/health`, reject invalid env at boot with non-zero exit |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":110,"content":"| `/app/server/health.js` | Pure handler building `{status:\"ok\", node_id}` (keeps routing thin for later middleware) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":111,"content":"| `/app/package.json` | `{ \"name\": \"huddle\", \"private\": true, \"main\": \"server/index.js\" }` — documents Node entry; **no required dependencies** for this task |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":121,"content":"| `/app/redis.conf` | Minimal conf: `bind 127.0.0.1`, `port 6379`, `dir /app/data/redis`, `protected-mode yes`, `save` optional; if omitted, pass equivalent flags on the `redis-server` CLI |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":126,"content":"1. `server/health.js` + `server/index.js` (can be verified with a one-off `NODE_ID=0 PORT=8000 node server/index.js` by the implementer—architect does not run the app).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":128,"content":"3. `start.sh` (depends on server entry existing)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":138,"content":"| Port/identity map | C2 | All HTTP/WS/SPA/IRC tasks |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":139,"content":"| Health | C1 | QA, optional SPA |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":151,"content":"| SPA `GET /` | MARATHON-21 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":162,"content":"| Empty `/app/data/` | Reserved; durable schema is MARATHON-3+ |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":168,"content":"| SPA shell and UI | MARATHON-21…23 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":181,"content":"| Redis already running on 6379 (foreign process) | `redis-server` fails; supervisor respawns Redis child. Log bind failure. Do not kill arbitrary PIDs outside children started by this `start.sh` (harness `marathon-freeports` is for verifiers, not the app). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":182,"content":"| HTTP node SIGKILL | Supervisor detects dead PID within poll interval and restarts that node only; other nodes and Redis keep running. New process must again serve correct `node_id`. Wall-clock from kill to successful health: **≤ 60s** |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":185,"content":"| `GET /api/health` during Redis outage | Still `200` + ok body |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":227,"content":"Auth, SPA, WS, IRC, message fan-out, multi-node data consistency.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":27,"totalMatchedLines":27,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-145d4db2-5737-4991-9181-030aa62bb3af-13\nfc_c1dfcd3d-f597-9174-b2c0-ae8e9bd5b6ae_3","startedAtMs":"1787428298933","completedAtMs":"1787428299002"},"model_call_id":"4dabf0fb-8eb4-4dfb-98f3-2bbb507fe57f-3-1bta","session_id":"0b561b47-2d17-430d-9c8e-044dfd49fd95","timestamp_ms":1787428299027}
