{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"started","call_id":"call-09ae3dfb-b301-450e-aaeb-138c230b4dbd-14\nfc_a798729c-bccd-99fc-9c37-d520f06024f0_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/marathon-3-design.md","offset":1,"limit":280}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-09ae3dfb-b301-450e-aaeb-138c230b4dbd-14\nfc_a798729c-bccd-99fc-9c37-d520f06024f0_0","startedAtMs":"1787428301236"},"model_call_id":"4dabf0fb-8eb4-4dfb-98f3-2bbb507fe57f-4-48zp","session_id":"0b561b47-2d17-430d-9c8e-044dfd49fd95","timestamp_ms":1787428301354}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-09ae3dfb-b301-450e-aaeb-138c230b4dbd-14\nfc_a798729c-bccd-99fc-9c37-d520f06024f0_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/tmp/marathon-3-design.md","offset":1,"limit":280},"result":{"success":{"content":"## Summary\n\nMARATHON-3 implements cluster-wide authentication for Huddle: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, and `GET /api/auth/me`, plus the shared durable user/token store that all three HTTP nodes read and write. It establishes the `UserObj` identity shape, opaque bearer tokens (`Authorization: Bearer …`), password hashing, username slug validation, and a reusable auth middleware that every later authenticated route (workspaces, channels, WS, IRC `PASS`, SPA) will call. Without this seam, no other feature can attribute callers or survive a request to a different node.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n- **Runtime:** Stay on the MARATHON-2 stack: Node.js stdlib `http` router in `server/index.js`, no Express/Fastify required.\n- **Durable shared store:** One **SQLite** database file at `/app/data/huddle.db`, opened by each HTTP worker via Node’s built-in **`node:sqlite` (`DatabaseSync`)**. Enable **WAL** + a non-zero `busy_timeout` so concurrent register/login from nodes 0/1/2 serialize safely. This is the authoritative store for users and sessions; **Redis is not used for auth durability** (Redis may be killed; users/tokens must survive).\n- **Passwords:** `crypto.scrypt` with a per-user random salt; store only `password_salt` + `password_hash` (never plaintext). Compare with timing-safe equality.\n- **Tokens:** Opaque random strings from `crypto.randomBytes` (≥16 chars when encoded; generate **32 bytes → base64url ≈ 43 chars**). Persist token → `user_id` in SQLite. Each successful register/login **issues a new token** (multiple concurrent sessions allowed). Tokens are looked up as presented; no JWT.\n- **IDs:** Stable cluster-wide `user.id` via `crypto.randomUUID()` (string UUID).\n- **Auth helper:** Export `authenticateRequest(req) → user | null` and/or middleware used by `/api/auth/me` and reserved for MARATHON-4+.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| Redis HASH for users/tokens | Not durable across Redis SIGKILL; epic requires cluster to keep working when Redis dies |\n| Per-node in-memory maps | Breaks “shared durable store across all three nodes”; register on :8000 would 401 on :8001 |\n| JWT without server-side session | Harder to revoke; contract only needs opaque bearer length ≥16; SQLite session rows are simpler and match IRC/WS token checks later |\n| npm `better-sqlite3` / Express | Unnecessary dependency; `node:sqlite` is available on Node 24 in this environment |\n| JSON file + flock only | Workable but weaker concurrency and no unique indexes for username race → prefer SQLite UNIQUE |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nSQLite file locking under three processes is simpler than a real DB server, but write throughput under heavy concurrent register is limited by WAL/busy waits. Acceptable for marathon scale. Using experimental `node:sqlite` avoids npm install in air-gapped/self-contained constraints; if the API shifts, implementer may pin Node flags or swap to an equivalent sync SQLite binding **without changing the HTTP contract**.\n\n### Conventions inherited from MARATHON-2 (authoritative)\n| Convention | Value |\n|------------|--------|\n| App root | `/app` |\n| HTTP entry | `server/index.js`, `NODE_ID` / `PORT` |\n| Durable root | `/app/data/` |\n| API prefix | `/api/...` |\n| JSON | `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8` |\n| Health | Unchanged; still Redis-independent |\n\n### Conventions fixed here (for siblings)\n| Convention | Value |\n|------------|--------|\n| DB path | `/app/data/huddle.db` (create parent dir if missing) |\n| `UserObj` public fields | `{id, username, display_name, timezone, avatar_url, status_text, status_emoji}` — always present on auth responses |\n| Username rules | Regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$` (letters, digits, underscore only; no spaces/hyphens/dots) |\n| Username uniqueness | Case-insensitive (`LOWER(username)` UNIQUE); store username with original casing from register |\n| Password | UTF-8 string length ≥ 8 (code units / JS `.length`); no other complexity rules |\n| Bearer | Header `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (single space); token string length ≥ 16 |\n| Error JSON | `{ \"error\": \"<string>\" }` for 400/401/409 (message text open; must be non-empty) |\n| No email | Register/login bodies must not require `email`; ignore unknown fields |\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared: `UserObj` (public; never include password/hash/salt/token)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<uuid-string>\",\n  \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n  \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n  \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n  \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Type | Nullability | Default on register |\n|-------|------|-------------|---------------------|\n| `id` | string (UUID) | required | generated |\n| `username` | string | required | from body |\n| `display_name` | string | required in responses | `display_name` if provided non-empty, else copy of `username` |\n| `timezone` | string | required in responses | `\"UTC\"` |\n| `avatar_url` | string | required in responses | `\"\"` |\n| `status_text` | string | required in responses | `\"\"` |\n| `status_emoji` | string | required in responses | `\"\"` |\n\n**Owner of mutations beyond register defaults:** MARATHON-4 (`PATCH /api/users/me`). This task only sets defaults so envelopes are complete.\n\n---\n\n### C1 — `POST /api/auth/register`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | None |\n| Request body | JSON `{ \"username\": string, \"password\": string, \"display_name\"?: string }` |\n| Success | `201` `{ \"user\": UserObj, \"token\": string }` |\n| Validation failure | `400` `{ \"error\": string }` — invalid/missing username, password &lt; 8, non-object body, wrong types |\n| Duplicate username | `409` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Content-Type in | Prefer `application/json`; empty/malformed JSON → `400` |\n\n**Server validation (authoritative):**\n1. Parse JSON object; missing `username` or `password` → `400`.\n2. `username` must match `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$` → else `400` (e.g. space, hyphen, empty).\n3. `password` must be string with `.length >= 8` → else `400`.\n4. Optional `display_name`: if present and not a string → `400`; if string, trim; empty after trim → treat as omitted (fall back to username).\n5. Insert user; UNIQUE conflict on case-insensitive username → `409`.\n6. Create session token; return `201`.\n\n**Client (SPA / MARATHON-21) while slow/failing:**\n- Disable submit / show pending on `auth-submit` until response.\n- On `201`: store `token` in `localStorage` key `huddle.token`; treat as logged-in; may call `GET /api/auth/me` or use returned `user`.\n- On `400`/`409`: show `error` string visibly in the auth form (no silent fail).\n- On network error / 5xx: show generic failure; do not clear unrelated UI state.\n- **MUST NOT** send an `email` field as required.\n\n**Who validates what:** Server is source of truth for slug/password/duplicate. Client may pre-check length for UX but must still handle server `400`/`409`.\n\n---\n\n### C2 — `POST /api/auth/login`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | None |\n| Request body | JSON `{ \"username\": string, \"password\": string }` |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj, \"token\": string }` |\n| Bad credentials | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` — wrong password **or** unknown username (same code; do not distinguish) |\n| Malformed body | `400` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n\n**Server:**\n1. Validate types/presence; malformed → `400`.\n2. Look up user by case-insensitive username; missing → `401` (same as bad password).\n3. Verify password with scrypt + stored salt; fail → `401`.\n4. Issue new token; return `200` with full `UserObj` (current profile fields from DB).\n\n**Client:** Same token storage and error surfacing as register. Wrong password must show a visible error, not navigate as success.\n\n---\n\n### C3 — `GET /api/auth/me`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required: `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |\n| Body | None |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` |\n| Missing/invalid/unknown token | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n\n**Header parsing:**\n- Require header matching `/^Bearer\\s+(\\S+)$/i` (trim); extract token.\n- Missing header, wrong scheme, empty token, or token not in DB → `401`.\n- Do not accept token via query string on this route (query `?token=` is SPA/WS concern later).\n\n**Client:** On app load, if `huddle.token` set, call `/api/auth/me`; on `401` clear token and show login; while pending, may show a loading shell without claiming a user.\n\n---\n\n### C4 — Cross-node durability (implicit contract)\n\nA user registered or token issued on any of `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` must be accepted by the other two within normal SQLite visibility (immediately after the successful response returns). QA will register on one port and `GET /api/auth/me` on another with the same token.\n\n---\n\n### C5 — Auth middleware seam (internal; for implementers of later tasks)\n\n```\nresolveBearerUser(authorizationHeader: string | null) → UserObj | null\nrequireUser(req, res) → UserObj | writes 401 and returns null\n```\n\n- Input: raw `Authorization` header value.\n- Output: public `UserObj` only.\n- Used by MARATHON-4+, MARATHON-5+, MARATHON-18 (`?token=` maps to same session table), MARATHON-20 (IRC `PASS <token>`).\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema change\n**New** SQLite DB `/app/data/huddle.db` (greenfield; backward compatible with empty `/app/data/`).\n\n#### Table `users`\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | UUID |\n| `username` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Original casing |\n| `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL UNIQUE | `lower(username)` for conflict/login |\n| `password_salt` | TEXT | NOT NULL | hex or base64 |\n| `password_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | scrypt output encoding |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\n\n#### Table `tokens`\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `token` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | Opaque bearer (≥16 chars) |\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\n\nIndexes: PK/UNIQUE as above; optional index `tokens(user_id)` for future logout-all (not required this task).\n\n**Migrations:** On worker boot, `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` + WAL pragmas. No versioned migration framework required yet; keep DDL in one module (`server/db.js`) so MARATHON-4+ can extend columns carefully.\n\n**Password material and salts never appear in HTTP responses.**\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.js` | Open `/app/data/huddle.db`, ensure `/app/data` exists, set `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout`, run DDL for `users`/`tokens`, export `getDb()` |\n| `server/auth/passwords.js` | `hashPassword(password) → {salt, hash}`, `verifyPassword(password, salt, hash) → boolean` using `crypto.scrypt` (sync or promisified consistently) |\n| `server/auth/tokens.js` | `issueToken(userId) → string` (insert row); `findUserIdByToken(token) → string \\| null` |\n| `server/auth/users.js` | `createUser(...)`, `findUserByUsername(username)`, `publicUser(row) → UserObj` |\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` | `resolveBearerUser`, `requireUser` |\n| `server/auth/routes.js` | Handlers for register, login, me; JSON parse helper; status codes per contract |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` (optional) | `readJson(req)`, `sendJson(res, status, body)` shared with health — only if not already present from MARATHON-2 |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/index.js` | Route `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me` before generic 404; keep `GET /api/health` behavior unchanged; initialize DB once at process start (fail boot if DB cannot open) |\n| `package.json` | No new dependencies required; may note Node ≥22 for `node:sqlite` |\n| `start.sh` | **No change required** if it already creates `/app/data` (MARATHON-2). If not yet implemented when this lands, ensure `mkdir -p /app/data` remains. Do not move Redis dir. |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness timer |\n| SPA / static HTML | MARATHON-21 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `db.js` + DDL  \n2. passwords / users / tokens  \n3. middleware  \n4. routes + wire `index.js`  \n5. Cross-node manual check (register :8000 → me :8001)\n\n### Parallelism\n- Backend implementer owns all files above.\n- Frontend MARATHON-21 **architecture** can proceed from contracts C1–C3; **implementation** of SPA auth UI should land after (or against mocked) these endpoints.\n- MARATHON-4 (profiles) extends `users` columns usage and adds routes; must reuse `UserObj` + `requireUser`.\n- MARATHON-5+ all depend on bearer middleware + durable users.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| C1/C2/C3 HTTP auth | MARATHON-21 SPA; QA grader |\n| `UserObj` shape | MARATHON-4, channel members, messages `author`, WS `user.updated` |\n| Session table / `resolveBearerUser` | MARATHON-5…20 authenticated APIs; WS `?token=`; IRC `PASS` |\n| `/app/data/huddle.db` | All durable domain tables (siblings add tables, do not fork a second user DB) |\n\n### Build order vs siblings\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-2 bootstrap (ports, `server/index.js`, `/app/data`). If MARATHON-2 is not merged, implementer still codes against its file layout and integrates when bootstrap lands.\n- **Blocks:** MARATHON-5, MARATHON-11, MARATHON-21 (declared dependents), and practically every authenticated task.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Profile GET/PATCH + field validation | MARATHON-4 |\n| Logout / token revoke endpoint | Not in API contract — SPA clears `huddle.token` only; optional later if needed |\n| WS token query param | MARATHON-18 |\n| IRC PASS | MARATHON-20 |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan of architect worktree, `/app`, and repo tree (baseline `timer.sh` only; MARATHON-2 design not yet implemented in tree):\n\n| Finding | Why excluded |\n|---------|----------------|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness utility |\n| `GET /api/health` / `start.sh` / Redis | MARATHON-2 |\n| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |\n| Workspaces / channels / messages / … | MARATHON-5+ |\n| SPA auth form, `huddle.token`, testids | MARATHON-21 (consumes C1–C3 only) |\n| WS `/api/ws?token=` | MARATHON-18 (reuse token table) |\n| IRC `PASS` / 464 | MARATHON-20 |\n| Redis pub/sub fan-out | MARATHON-18/19 |\n| Explicit logout API / token expiry TTL | Not in grader auth contract |\n| Email verification, OAuth, Slack SDK | Prohibited / not specified |\n| Rate limiting / CAPTCHA | Not required |\n\nNo existing `/api/auth` code or username references in-repo to update.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":348,"fileSize":19531,"path":"/tmp/marathon-3-design.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":280},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-09ae3dfb-b301-450e-aaeb-138c230b4dbd-14\nfc_a798729c-bccd-99fc-9c37-d520f06024f0_0","startedAtMs":"1787428301236","completedAtMs":"1787428301374"},"model_call_id":"4dabf0fb-8eb4-4dfb-98f3-2bbb507fe57f-4-48zp","session_id":"0b561b47-2d17-430d-9c8e-044dfd49fd95","timestamp_ms":1787428301398}
