ata show MARATHON-21 --output json | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"comments:\", d.get(\"comments\")); print(\"keys:\", list(d.keys()))'","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"Three-pane layout (sidebar + messages + on-demand thread). Coloured sidebar, workspace identity, #channel names, channel header name+topic. Channel list/create/switch/duplicate validation. Message post/edit/delete via hover toolbar with edited indicator; persist across hard reload; empty-message validation; empty-channel non-blank copy. Message rows: avatar+author+human timestamp+body. Pin all listed channel/message/workspace testids and data-channel-id/name attrs.\n---\n\nThread opens in right-side panel; parent shows N replies. Reactions via emoji-picker grid (not prompt()) with reaction-chip counts. Workspace/channel settings modals, members, invitations UI with all remaining pinned testids and modal DOM ids.\n---\n\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-22T19:51:44.873Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:44.900Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\n","executionTime":202,"interleavedOutput":"time=2026-08-22T19:51:44.873Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\nThree-pane layout (sidebar + messages + on-demand thread). Coloured sidebar, workspace identity, #channel names, channel header name+topic. Channel list/create/switch/duplicate validation. Message post/edit/delete via hover toolbar with edited indicator; persist across hard reload; empty-message validation; empty-channel non-blank copy. Message rows: avatar+author+human timestamp+body. Pin all listed channel/message/workspace testids and data-channel-id/name attrs.\n---\n\ntime=2026-08-22T19:51:44.900Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\nThread opens in right-side panel; parent shows N replies. Reactions via emoji-picker grid (not prompt()) with reaction-chip counts. Workspace/channel settings modals, members, invitations UI with all remaining pinned testids and modal DOM ids.\n---\n\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help            help for data\n  -o, --output string   Output format: text|json (default \"text\")\n      --server string   Loom server base URL (or LOOM_SERVER_URL env var)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --backend string      AI backend CLI to use (codex, claude, opencode). Env: LOOM_BACKEND\n      --log-format string   Log format (text|json) (default \"text\")\n      --log-output string   Log output destination (stderr|<filepath>) (default \"stderr\")\n      --workspace string    Workspace ID. Env: LOOM_WORKSPACE\n\nUse \"loom data [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n","localExecutionTimeMs":112},"isBackground":false},"description":"Show dependent SPA tasks and comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-09ae3dfb-b301-450e-aaeb-138c230b4dbd-19\nfc_a798729c-bccd-99fc-9c37-d520f06024f0_5","startedAtMs":"1787428304758","completedAtMs":"1787428304961"},"model_call_id":"4dabf0fb-8eb4-4dfb-98f3-2bbb507fe57f-4-48zp","session_id":"0b561b47-2d17-430d-9c8e-044dfd49fd95","timestamp_ms":1787428304989}
