{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-78e1c035-369e-467d-b69e-17750c0d2c3a-15\nfc_9c407e55-96f7-96c4-bb25-b0021178f9aa_1","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/33e06cea-2423-450c-b7d1-47b1dd4595df.txt","offset":400,"limit":650},"result":{"success":{"content":"resolveBearerUser(authorizationHeader: string | null) → UserObj | null\nrequireUser(req, res) → UserObj | writes 401 and returns null\n```\n\n- Input: raw `Authorization` header value.\n- Output: public `UserObj` only.\n- Used by MARATHON-4+, MARATHON-5+, MARATHON-18 (`?token=` maps to same session table), MARATHON-20 (IRC `PASS <token>`).\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema change\n**New** SQLite DB `/app/data/huddle.db` (greenfield; backward compatible with empty `/app/data/`).\n\n#### Table `users`\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | UUID |\n| `username` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Original casing |\n| `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL UNIQUE | `lower(username)` for conflict/login |\n| `password_salt` | TEXT | NOT NULL | hex or base64 |\n| `password_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | scrypt output encoding |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\n\n#### Table `tokens`\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `token` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | Opaque bearer (≥16 chars) |\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\n\nIndexes: PK/UNIQUE as above; optional index `tokens(user_id)` for future logout-all (not required this task).\n\n**Migrations:** On worker boot, `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` + WAL pragmas. No versioned migration framework required yet; keep DDL in one module (`server/db.js`) so MARATHON-4+ can extend columns carefully.\n\n**Password material and salts never appear in HTTP responses.**\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.js` | Open `/app/data/huddle.db`, ensure `/app/data` exists, set `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout`, run DDL for `users`/`tokens`, export `getDb()` |\n| `server/auth/passwords.js` | `hashPassword(password) → {salt, hash}`, `verifyPassword(password, salt, hash) → boolean` using `crypto.scrypt` (sync or promisified consistently) |\n| `server/auth/tokens.js` | `issueToken(userId) → string` (insert row); `findUserIdByToken(token) → string \\| null` |\n| `server/auth/users.js` | `createUser(...)`, `findUserByUsername(username)`, `publicUser(row) → UserObj` |\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` | `resolveBearerUser`, `requireUser` |\n| `server/auth/routes.js` | Handlers for register, login, me; JSON parse helper; status codes per contract |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` (optional) | `readJson(req)`, `sendJson(res, status, body)` shared with health — only if not already present from MARATHON-2 |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/index.js` | Route `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me` before generic 404; keep `GET /api/health` behavior unchanged; initialize DB once at process start (fail boot if DB cannot open) |\n| `package.json` | No new dependencies required; may note Node ≥22 for `node:sqlite` |\n| `start.sh` | **No change required** if it already creates `/app/data` (MARATHON-2). If not yet implemented when this lands, ensure `mkdir -p /app/data` remains. Do not move Redis dir. |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness timer |\n| SPA / static HTML | MARATHON-21 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `db.js` + DDL  \n2. passwords / users / tokens  \n3. middleware  \n4. routes + wire `index.js`  \n5. Cross-node manual check (register :8000 → me :8001)\n\n### Parallelism\n- Backend implementer owns all files above.\n- Frontend MARATHON-21 **architecture** can proceed from contracts C1–C3; **implementation** of SPA auth UI should land after (or against mocked) these endpoints.\n- MARATHON-4 (profiles) extends `users` columns usage and adds routes; must reuse `UserObj` + `requireUser`.\n- MARATHON-5+ all depend on bearer middleware + durable users.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| C1/C2/C3 HTTP auth | MARATHON-21 SPA; QA grader |\n| `UserObj` shape | MARATHON-4, channel members, messages `author`, WS `user.updated` |\n| Session table / `resolveBearerUser` | MARATHON-5…20 authenticated APIs; WS `?token=`; IRC `PASS` |\n| `/app/data/huddle.db` | All durable domain tables (siblings add tables, do not fork a second user DB) |\n\n### Build order vs siblings\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-2 bootstrap (ports, `server/index.js`, `/app/data`). If MARATHON-2 is not merged, implementer still codes against its file layout and integrates when bootstrap lands.\n- **Blocks:** MARATHON-5, MARATHON-11, MARATHON-21 (declared dependents), and practically every authenticated task.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Profile GET/PATCH + field validation | MARATHON-4 |\n| Logout / token revoke endpoint | Not in API contract — SPA clears `huddle.token` only; optional later if needed |\n| WS token query param | MARATHON-18 |\n| IRC PASS | MARATHON-20 |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan of architect worktree, `/app`, and repo tree (baseline `timer.sh` only; MARATHON-2 design not yet implemented in tree):\n\n| Finding | Why excluded |\n|---------|----------------|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness utility |\n| `GET /api/health` / `start.sh` / Redis | MARATHON-2 |\n| `GET /api/users/{id}`, `PATCH /api/users/me` | MARATHON-4 |\n| Workspaces / channels / messages / … | MARATHON-5+ |\n| SPA auth form, `huddle.token`, testids | MARATHON-21 (consumes C1–C3 only) |\n| WS `/api/ws?token=` | MARATHON-18 (reuse token table) |\n| IRC `PASS` / 464 | MARATHON-20 |\n| Redis pub/sub fan-out | MARATHON-18/19 |\n| Explicit logout API / token expiry TTL | Not in grader auth contract |\n| Email verification, OAuth, Slack SDK | Prohibited / not specified |\n| Rate limiting / CAPTCHA | Not required |\n\nNo existing `/api/auth` code or username references in-repo to update.\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Username `\"alice\"` then `\"Alice\"` | Second register → `409` (case-insensitive unique) |\n| Login with d\n---DESCRIPTION---\nImplement POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, GET /api/auth/me per API contract. Username slug rules, password >=8, 201/200 envelopes {user,token} or {user}, 400/401/409 as specified. Token length >=16. Shared durable store across all three nodes.\n\n======== MARATHON-4 ========\ntime=2026-08-22T19:54:22.959Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntitle: Profiles: GET user and PATCH /api/users/me\nlabels: ['backend']\nstatus: blocked\nnotes: BLOCKED: Depends on MARATHON-3 (users table, requireUser, publicUser, auth middleware). MARATHON-3 is still in_progress and has not landed on main/harness-integrated head; this worktree only has MARATHON-2 bootstrap (no server/auth). Re-claim after MARATHON-3 merges.\n---DESIGN---\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-4 adds authenticated profile read and self-update on top of the MARATHON-3 `UserObj` / `users` table: `GET /api/users/{id}` returns a public profile (`200` / `404`), and `PATCH /api/users/me` mutates a validated subset of profile fields (`400` on bad timezone or over-length strings). Successful patches persist in the shared SQLite store (visible on every node) and emit a cluster-wide `user.updated` event through a no-op-safe broadcast hook that MARATHON-18 wires to WebSocket fan-out. This closes the gap between register-time profile defaults and live profile editing the SPA/settings flows need.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n- **Reuse MARATHON-3 identity stack:** Same `/app/data/huddle.db` `users` row, same `publicUser(row) → UserObj`, same `requireUser` / bearer middleware. No second user store.\n- **Routes live under `/api/users`:** New module `server/users/routes.js` (HTTP only). Persistence helpers (`findUserById`, `updateUserProfile`) extend `server/auth/users.js` so DDL ownership stays with auth.\n- **Mutable PATCH subset only:** `display_name`, `timezone`, `avatar_url`, `status_text`, `status_emoji`. **Never** allow `id`, `username`, password fields, or token mutation via this route.\n- **Timezone validation:** Accept only IANA time zone names. Prefer `Intl.supportedValuesOf('timeZone')` when available (Node 20+); otherwise validate by constructing `new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { timeZone })` and rejecting on throw. `\"UTC\"` remains valid. Do **not** invent offset-only strings like `\"UTC+1\"` as valid unless they appear in the IANA list.\n- **Length caps (authoritative):** enforce on the server with JS string `.length` (same length model as MARATHON-3 passwords).\n- **WS hook, not WS implementation:** After a successful DB commit, call `emitUserUpdated(userObj)` from `server/events/userUpdated.js`. Default export is a no-op (or in-process listener list). MARATHON-18 replaces/registers the real global WS broadcast. HTTP success **must not** depend on Redis or WS being up.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| Return bare `UserObj` without `{ \"user\": ... }` wrapper | Breaks symmetry with `GET /api/auth/me` and register/login envelopes fixed in MARATHON-3 |\n| Allow PATCH to rename `username` | Username is the durable login identity (case-insensitive unique); renaming needs a separate task and migration story |\n| Require workspace membership to GET a user | Workspaces are MARATHON-5; until then any authenticated user may resolve any `user.id` (global directory) |\n| Put profile columns in a separate `profiles` table | Unnecessary join; MARATHON-3 already defined columns on `users` |\n| Block PATCH until MARATHON-18 ships | Task explicitly says hook up when WS exists; profile REST must work without WS |\n| Soft-validate timezone (accept any string) | Task requires timezone validation → `400` |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nGlobal directory lookup (any authed user → any user id) is simpler than workspace-scoped visibility but leaks existence of all accounts by UUID. Acceptable for this marathon; MARATHON-5+ may tighten visibility later without changing `UserObj` shape.\n\n### Conventions inherited (authoritative)\n| Source | Convention |\n|--------|------------|\n| MARATHON-2 | `/app`, `server/index.js`, `/api/...`, JSON `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`, three nodes, `/app/data/` |\n| MARATHON-3 | `UserObj` seven fields; error `{ \"error\": string }`; bearer `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; SQLite `/app/data/huddle.db`; `requireUser`; ignore unknown JSON keys on write |\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### Shared: `UserObj` (unchanged from MARATHON-3)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<uuid-string>\",\n  \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n  \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n  \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n  \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n  \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n}\n```\n\nAll seven keys always present in responses. Never include password, hash, salt, or token.\n\n### Patchable field limits (server-authoritative)\n\n| Field | Type | Max `.length` | Empty string | Notes |\n|-------|------|---------------|--------------|-------|\n| `display_name` | string | 64 | allowed | Trim leading/trailing whitespace before length check and store; empty after trim → store `\"\"` |\n| `timezone` | string | 64 (and IANA-valid) | **not** allowed | Must be non-empty IANA name (e.g. `UTC`, `America/New_York`) |\n| `avatar_url` | string | 2048 | allowed | No scheme check required; store as given after type check (do not trim interior spaces) |\n| `status_text` | string | 100 | allowed | Trim ends; empty → `\"\"` |\n| `status_emoji` | string | 32 | allowed | Trim ends; empty → `\"\"`; multi-codepoint emoji OK within length |\n\n**Partial update semantics:** Only keys **present** in the JSON object are updated. Omitted keys stay unchanged. Wrong type (`null`, number, object, array) for a present key → `400`. Empty object `{}` → `200` with unchanged `UserObj` (no WS emit if nothing changed).\n\n**Forbidden keys if present with any value:** `id`, `username`, `password`, `password_hash`, `password_salt`, `token` → `400` `{ \"error\": string }` (do not silently ignore identity/credential fields).\n\nOther unknown keys → ignore (same as MARATHON-3 register).\n\n---\n\n### C1 — `GET /api/users/{id}`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required (`requireUser`) |\n| Path param | `id` — opaque user UUID string (exact match to `users.id`) |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` |\n| Not found | `404` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Unauthenticated | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Wrong method | `405` or `404`; must not `500` |\n\n**Server:**\n1. Resolve bearer → user or `401`.\n2. If path is exactly `/api/users/me` on GET: treat `id` as the literal string `me` → **404** (self profile remains `GET /api/auth/me`). Do not special-case.\n3. Look up `users.id = id`; missing → `404`.\n4. Return `publicUser` envelope.\n\n**Who validates:** Server owns UUID existence. Client must not assume every id from messages still exists.\n\n**Client (SPA / MARATHON-21–23) while slow/failing:**\n- While pending: keep prior cached profile or show a neutral placeholder; do not flash logged-out.\n- On `200`: render `user.display_name` (fallback UX: `username` if display_name empty).\n- On `404`: show “user not found”; do not clear session.\n- On `401`: clear `huddle.token`, show login (same as `/api/auth/me`).\n- On network/5xx: show transient error; retry allowed.\n\n---\n\n### C2 — `PATCH /api/users/me`\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Auth | Required (`requireUser`) — updates **only** the authenticated user |\n| Body | JSON object; subset of patchable fields above |\n| Success | `200` `{ \"user\": UserObj }` (post-update row) |\n| Validation failure | `400` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Unauthenticated | `401` `{ \"error\": string }` |\n| Malformed JSON / non-object | `400` |\n\n**Server algorithm:**\n1. `requireUser` or `401`.\n2. `readJson` → must be a plain object.\n3. Validate each present key per table; collect updates.\n4. If any forbidden key present → `400` before writes.\n5. If updates non-empty: `UPDATE users SET ... WHERE id = ?` in SQLite; re-read row; `publicUser`.\n6. If at least one field actually changed: call `emitUserUpdated(userObj)` (best-effort; errors logged, HTTP still `200`).\n7. If no fields changed: return `200` with current user; **do not** emit.\n\n**Who validates:** Server is source of truth for IANA timezone and lengths. Client may pre-check for UX but must handle `400`.\n\n**Client while slow/failing:**\n- Disable save control / show pending on profile form until response.\n- Optimistic UI optional; on `400` revert fields and show `error` string.\n- On `200`: replace local current-user state with returned `user`; also expect eventual `user.updated` WS (when MARATHON-18 exists) and reconcile by `user.id`.\n- On `401`: logout flow.\n- On network/5xx: keep form dirty state; show retry; **MUST NOT** assume server applied the patch.\n\n---\n\n### C3 — `user.updated` broadcast seam (owned here; delivered by MARATHON-18)\n\n**Event name:** `user.updated`  \n**Scope:** Global — all authenticated WS connections on all nodes (when hub exists), not channel-scoped.  \n**Payload (WS frame / hub message body):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"user.updated\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": \"<uuid>\",\n    \"username\": \"<slug>\",\n    \"display_name\": \"<string>\",\n    \"timezone\": \"<string>\",\n    \"avatar_url\": \"<string>\",\n    \"status_text\": \"<string>\",\n    \"status_emoji\": \"<string>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Module contract:**\n\n```\n// server/events/userUpdated.js\nemitUserUpdated(user: UserObj): void\nregisterUserUpdatedListener(fn: (user: UserObj) => void): void  // optional helper for tests / WS hub\n```\n\n- MARATHON-4 always calls `emitUserUpdated` after a mutating PATCH.\n- Until MARATHON-18 registers a listener / Redis publish, emit is a no-op (in-process listeners only if registered).\n- MARATHON-18/19 own cross-node fan-out; this task does **not** publish to Redis directly (avoids inventing the pub/sub envelope twice). If implementer prefers a tiny in-process EventEmitter only, that is enough for C3.\n\n**Client when WS exists:** On `user.updated`, update any rendered profile/message author chrome for matching `user.id`. If WS is down, HTTP GET/PATCH remain correct; stale UI until refresh is acceptable.\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema change\n**None required** if MARATHON-3 DDL already created:\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT PK | NOT NULL | Immutable via PATCH |\n| `username` / `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Immutable via PATCH |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Mutable |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | Mutable; IANA |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | Mutable |\n| password / salt / `created_at` | — | — | Untouched |\n\n**Backward compatibility:** Additive routes only. Existing auth responses keep working. No column drops/renames.\n\n**If MARATHON-3 columns are somehow missing** (partial implement): implementer adds the same `ALTER TABLE` / DDL defaults as MARATHON-3 — do not invent alternate names.\n\nNo new tables.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/users/routes.js` | Handlers: `GET /api/users/:id`, `PATCH /api/users/me`; path parse; status codes per C1/C2; call validation + store + `emitUserUpdated` |\n| `server/users/validate.js` | `assertPatchBody(obj) → { updates } \\| { error }` — length, type, IANA timezone, forbidden keys |\n| `server/events/userUpdated.js` | `emitUserUpdated`, optional `registerUserUpdatedListener`; default no-op fan-out |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/users.js` | Add `findUserById(id) → row \\| null`, `updateUserProfile(id, updates) → row` (UPDATE only provided columns); keep `publicUser` as single serializer |\n| `server/index.js` | After auth routes: dispatch `PATCH` `/api/users/me` and `GET` `/api/users/*` before generic 404; keep health + auth behavior unchanged |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Reuse `readJson` / `sendJson` if MARATHON-3 added them; otherwise use the same helpers auth routes use (do not duplicate divergent JSON error shapes) |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` / `redis.conf` / health | MARATHON-2 |\n| `server/auth/routes.js` register/login/me contracts | Unchanged; PATCH is not `/api/auth/me` |\n| SPA / static UI | MARATHON-21–23 |\n| WS router / Redis pubsub | MARATHON-18/19 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `findUserById` / `updateUserProfile` + validator  \n2. `userUpdated` event stub  \n3. HTTP routes + `index.js` wiring  \n4. Cross-node check: PATCH on :8000 → GET user on :8001  \n\n### Parallelism\n- Backend-only implementation.\n- Frontend settings UI (MARATHON-23) can be designed against C2; implement against live API after this lands.\n- MARATHON-18 can implement WS listen/subscribe in parallel using C3 payload; must call `registerUserUpdatedListener` or equivalent from the hub boot.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| C1 GET user by id | Messages/members UIs; mentions; SPA profile popovers |\n| C2 PATCH `/api/users/me` | SPA settings (MARATHON-23); any client editing status/timezone |\n| C3 `user.updated` payload + `emitUserUpdated` | MARATHON-18 WS global broadcast; MARATHON-19 fan-out must carry this event type when Redis is down |\n| Length/IANA rules | All writers of profile fields (no other writer should bypass validator) |\n\n### Build order vs siblings\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-3 (`users` table, `requireUser`, `publicUser`). MARATHON-2 for process topology.\n- **Soft-blocked on WS delivery:** none for HTTP acceptance; WS delivery blocked on MARATHON-18.\n- **Does not block:** workspace/channel CRUD can proceed; they should embed `UserObj` via `publicUser` when returning members.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Actual WS subscribe + global emit over Redis | MARATHON-18 / MARATHON-19 |\n| SPA profile/settings forms + testids | MARATHON-21 / MARATHON-23 |\n| Username change / password change APIs | New task if ever required |\n| Workspace-scoped profile visibility | Optional later under MARATHON-5+ |\n| Avatar file upload | MARATHON-11 (files); this task only stores URL string |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan (architect worktree = baseline `timer.sh` only; sibling `backend-dev-1` has MARATHON-2 `server/index.js`, `server/health.js`, `start.sh`, tests — **no** `/api/users` or auth modules yet; `/app` same baseline; grep for `UserObj` / `timezone` / `user.updated` / `/api/users` → no implementation hits):\n\n| Finding | Why excluded |\n|---------|----------------|\n| `server/health.js`, `GET /api/health`, `start.sh`, Redis | MARATHON-2 |\n| `POST /api/auth/*`, `GET /api/auth/me`, token/password DDL | MARATHON-3 (prerequisite; do not re-specify) |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\n| WS `/api/ws`, dense seq, resume | MARATHON-18 |\n| Redis-down fan-out | MARATHON-19 |\n| IRC nick/profile bridging | MARATHON-20 |\n| SPA auth + settings UI | MARATHON-21–23 |\n| File upload for avatars | MARATHON-11 |\n| Workspaces/members embedding users | MARATHON-5 |\n| Rate limiting profile writes | Not required |\n\n## Edge Cases & Error Handling\n\n| Situation | Expected behavior |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| GET unknown UUID | `404` `{error}` |\n| GET valid id without auth | `401` |\n| GET `/api/users/me` | `404` (literal id `me`); use `/api/auth/me` |\n| PATCH without auth | `401` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"Not/AZone\"` | `400` |\n| PATCH `timezone: \"\"` | `400` |\n| PATCH `display_name` length 65 | `400` |\n| PATCH `status_text` length 101 | `400` |\n| PATCH `status_emoji` length 33 | `400` |\n| PATCH `avatar_url` length 2049 | `400` |\n| PATCH includes `username` | `400` (forbidden key) |\n| PATCH includes only unknown keys | Treat as `{}` → `200`, no emit |\n| PATCH `display_name: \"  Alice  \"` | Store `\"Alice\"` (trim\n---DESCRIPTION---\nUserObj fields {id,username,display_name,timezone,avatar_url,status_text,status_emoji}. GET /api/users/{id} → 200/404. PATCH /api/users/me accepts subset, validates timezone/lengths → 400. Profile updates broadcast WS user.updated globally (hook up when WS exists).\n\n======== MARATHON-21 ========\ntime=2026-08-22T19:54:22.998Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\ntitle: SPA shell: auth UI, token storage, logout/login\nlabels: ['frontend']\nstatus: open\nnotes: Design complete for SPA shell auth UI. Consumes MARATHON-3 C1–C3; static public/ served from GET / on every node; huddle.token + pinned testids; logout is client-only. Handing to review (frontend implementer after architect label cleared). Cross-port localStorage is origin-scoped — not required.\n---DESIGN---\n## Summary\n\nMARATHON-21 delivers the Huddle browser shell: every HTTP node serves a same-origin SPA at `GET /`, and that SPA owns sign-up/login UI, visible validation errors, auto-login after success, session restore via `localStorage` key `huddle.token`, and logout that returns the user to the auth modal. It consumes the already-landed MARATHON-3 contracts (`POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me`) without adding auth APIs, and leaves a documented authenticated-shell mount point for MARATHON-22 (workspaces/channels/messages) and MARATHON-23 (threads/settings). Pinned DOM hooks (`data-testid` / `id`) make the auth flow automatable at **1280×900**.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n1. **Static SPA assets under `/app/public/`**, served by each Node worker with stdlib `fs` + `http` (no Express, no bundler, no npm frontend deps). Entry document is `public/index.html`; client logic in `public/js/auth.js` + `public/js/app.js`; styles in `public/css/app.css`. Scripts load as classic or deferred `<script src=\"…\">` (no build step in `start.sh`).\n2. **Same-origin `fetch`** to `/api/auth/*` with `Content-Type: application/json`. Token persistence **only** at `localStorage['huddle.token']` (exact key per MARATHON-3). Authenticated calls send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.\n3. **Client-owned logout:** clear `huddle.token`, clear in-memory session/user, show `#auth-modal`. No `POST /api/auth/logout` (explicitly out of MARATHON-3; server tokens may remain until a future revoke task).\n4. **Two UI phases in this task only:**\n   - **Unauthenticated:** `#auth-modal` visible with sign-up **or** login form (toggled by `auth-toggle`).\n   - **Authenticated shell:** modal hidden; chrome shows `current-user` + `logout-btn`; a `#app-shell` placeholder hosts future MARATHON-22 content (empty or minimal “signed in” copy is fine; **must not** invent workspace/channel APIs here).\n5. **Boot sequence:** on `DOMContentLoaded`, if `huddle.token` is set → `GET /api/auth/me` → success enters shell with returned `user`; `401`/network failure clears token and shows auth modal. Register/login success writes token then enters shell using the response `user` (auto-login; optional immediate `/me` is allowed but not required).\n\n### Alternatives considered\n| Alternative | Why rejected |\n|-------------|--------------|\n| React/Vite/Webpack SPA | Needs install + build; epic requires self-contained `/app` with no remote services; MARATHON-2/3 used zero npm deps |\n| Server-rendered login forms | Task asks for SPA shell and client `localStorage`; SSR would fight MARATHON-22 client routing |\n| Cookie/`HttpOnly` sessions | MARATHON-3 fixed opaque Bearer + `huddle.token`; changing storage breaks the declared SPA/WS/IRC token story |\n| Serve SPA only from node 0 | Task: “on any node”; QA may hit `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` interchangeably |\n| Implement workspace restore UI here | Belongs to MARATHON-22; this task only restores **auth session** and clears shell state so 22 can reload domain data after re-login |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nA vanilla multi-file SPA is less ergonomic than a framework, but keeps the cluster zero-dependency and matches the existing Node stdlib style. Client-only logout leaves orphaned token rows in SQLite; acceptable until an explicit revoke endpoint is tasked.\n\n### Conventions inherited (authoritative)\n| Source | Convention |\n|--------|------------|\n| MARATHON-2 | App root `/app`; HTTP `server/index.js`; ports `8000+NODE_ID`; API under `/api/...`; JSON `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`; browser UI at **`GET /`** (disk path `/app` ≠ URL path) |\n| MARATHON-3 | `UserObj` seven string fields; register/login/me envelopes; errors `{ \"error\": string }`; username `^[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,32}$`; password length ≥ 8; `huddle.token`; Bearer header; no email required |\n| MARATHON-4 (design only) | Future profile PATCH; on `401` clear `huddle.token` and show login — same logout path this shell owns |\n\n### Conventions fixed here (for siblings)\n| Convention | Value |\n|------------|--------|\n| Static root | `/app/public/` (repo path `public/`) |\n| Token storage key | `localStorage` key **`huddle.token`** exactly (string token only; do not store full `UserObj` as the session source of truth) |\n| Auth modal | Element **`id=\"auth-modal\"`** |\n| Pinned testids | `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`, `current-user`, `logout-btn` |\n| Auth mode toggle | `auth-toggle` switches register ↔ login **without** navigation |\n| Display identity | `current-user` text content = `user.display_name` (fallback `user.username` if empty) |\n| Shell mount | `#app-shell` (or equivalent stable id) — MARATHON-22 attaches three-pane UI here; must exist when authenticated |\n| Viewport | Primary layout usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scroll for auth chrome |\n| Asset URLs | Absolute-from-root paths `/css/...`, `/js/...` so any node origin works |\n\n## Interface Contracts\n\n### C-SPA-1 — `GET /` (and static assets) — **Backend owns serve; Frontend owns behavior**\n\n| | |\n|--|--|\n| Method / path | `GET /` |\n| Auth | None |\n| Success | `200`, `Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8`, body = SPA document that loads CSS/JS |\n| Other methods on `/` | `405` `{ \"error\": \"method_not_allowed\" }` **or** `404` JSON; must not `500` |\n\n**Also serve (same task):**\n| Path | Type | Notes |\n|------|------|-------|\n| `GET /css/app.css` | `text/css; charset=utf-8` | From `public/css/app.css` |\n| `GET /js/app.js`, `GET /js/auth.js` (and any other files under `public/js/`) | `application/javascript; charset=utf-8` | Path traversal forbidden |\n| `GET /` only as HTML entry | — | Do **not** require `/index.html` for acceptance; optional redirect/`index.html` alias is allowed |\n\n**Routing order in `server/index.js` (must preserve API contracts):**\n1. `GET /api/health` (unchanged)\n2. Auth API via `handleAuthRoutes` (unchanged)\n3. Static / SPA handler for safe paths under `public/`\n4. Else `404` `{ \"error\": \"not_found\" }`\n\n**Path safety:** resolve files under `path.join(__dirname, '..', 'public')` (or `/app/public`); reject `..` segments; never serve outside `public/`. Missing file → `404` JSON (same envelope as today) or plain 404 — not `500`.\n\n**Client while slow:** N/A for document fetch beyond browser load; if CSS/JS 404, auth UI may be unstyled but HTML structure with testids must still be present in the HTML (prefer embedding critical hooks in `index.html`).\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-2 — Client → `POST /api/auth/register` (consume MARATHON-3 C1)\n\n| Client sends | `{ \"username\": string, \"password\": string, \"display_name\"?: string }` |\n| Success | `201` `{ \"user\": UserObj, \"token\": string }` |\n| Errors | `400` / `409` / `5xx` with `{ \"error\": string }` when provided |\n\n**Client ownership:**\n- Serialize JSON; **MUST NOT** require or gate on `email`.\n- On submit: disable `auth-submit` (or equivalent pending state) until response settles.\n- On `201`: `localStorage.setItem('huddle.token', token)`; set current user from `user`; hide `#auth-modal`; show authenticated chrome (**auto-login**).\n- On `400`/`409`: show `error` string **visibly** inside the auth form (dedicated error element adjacent to the form; must be readable without opening DevTools).\n- On network failure / `5xx`: show a visible generic message (e.g. “Something went wrong”); do not clear an existing valid token unless this was not a logged-in flow.\n- Optional client pre-check (username regex / password length) may run before fetch; **server remains authoritative** — still handle server errors.\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-3 — Client → `POST /api/auth/login` (consume MARATHON-3 C2)\n\nSame as register for storage and error visibility; success status is `200`. Wrong password / unknown user → `401` → visible error; **MUST NOT** enter authenticated shell.\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-4 — Client → `GET /api/auth/me` (consume MARATHON-3 C3)\n\n| When | App boot if `huddle.token` present; optionally after login |\n| Header | `Authorization: Bearer <token>` |\n| Success `200` | Enter shell with `user`; keep token |\n| `401` | `localStorage.removeItem('huddle.token')`; show `#auth-modal`; clear `current-user` |\n| Network / `5xx` while booting with a token | Show auth modal **or** a non-claiming loading state, then fall back to auth modal; **MUST NOT** leave a forged `current-user` without a successful `/me` or prior successful register/login in this page life. Prefer: treat boot failure like logged-out after clear-or-keep policy — **decision: on boot network/`5xx`, keep token in storage but show a visible retry/error in the modal region and do not mark user logged-in; user can retry or clear via attempting login. On `401`, always clear token.** |\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-5 — Logout / re-login (client-only)\n\n| Action | Behavior |\n|--------|----------|\n| Click `logout-btn` | Remove `huddle.token`; clear in-memory `user` and any shell selection state this task owns; hide authenticated chrome; show `#auth-modal` in **login** mode; clear password fields |\n| Login again (same or other user) | On `200`, store new token, show shell with new `user` |\n| “Restores workspace” meaning for **this** task | Re-entering the authenticated shell after logout→login (and after hard reload with valid token). **Domain** workspace/channel/message tree reload is **MARATHON-22**: this task exposes a stable “session became authenticated” / “session cleared” seam (e.g. `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('huddle:auth', { detail: { user } }))` and `huddle:logout`) so 22 can refetch. Until 22 lands, shell may be empty — that is success for 21 |\n\n**MUST NOT:** call a non-existent logout API; leave `huddle.token` set after logout; show `current-user` while modal is the active unauthenticated UI.\n\n---\n\n### C-SPA-6 — DOM contract (QA / Playwright)\n\nExact attributes (implementer must not rename):\n\n| Hook | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| `#auth-modal` | Present in DOM; visible when logged out; not the primary interactive surface when logged in (hidden via CSS `display:none` / `hidden` attribute / equivalent) |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-form\"]` | The sign-up/login `<form>` inside the modal |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-submit\"]` | Submit control (button or input) |\n| `[data-testid=\"auth-toggle\"]` | Control that switches between Sign up and Log in modes |\n| `[data-testid=\"current-user\"]` | Visible when authenticated; text identifies the user (`display_name`) |\n| `[data-testid=\"logout-btn\"]` | Visible when authenticated; triggers C-SPA-5 |\n\nForm fields (recommended stable hooks for typing; if not testid-pinned by task, use `name` attributes):\n- `name=\"username\"`, `name=\"password\"`\n- Optional `name=\"display_name\"` visible **only** in sign-up mode\n\nError surface: an element inside `#auth-modal` / `auth-form` that displays the latest error string (e.g. `data-testid=\"auth-error\"` is **recommended** for clarity but **not** required by the task text — if omitted, error text must still be visible in the modal).\n\n## Data Model\n\n### Server schema\n**No SQLite / API schema changes.** Reuses MARATHON-3 `users` / `tokens` and `UserObj`.\n\n### Browser persistence\n| Key | Type | Nullability | Notes |\n|-----|------|-------------|-------|\n| `localStorage['huddle.token']` | string | absent when logged out | Opaque bearer ≥16 chars from API; never store password |\n| In-memory `currentUser` | `UserObj` \\| null | null when logged out | Rebuilt from register/login/`/me`; not the durability source |\n\n### Backward compatibility\nAdding `GET /` HTML where unknown paths previously returned JSON `404` is an intentional behavior change for `/` and static paths only. All `/api/*` contracts remain unchanged.\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `public/index.html` | SPA shell: `#auth-modal`, form with pinned testids, `#app-shell`, links to CSS/JS |\n| `public/css/app.css` | Layout for auth modal + minimal authenticated chrome; usable at 1280×900 |\n| `public/js/auth.js` | Token get/set/clear; `register` / `login` / `me` fetch helpers; Bearer header helper |\n| `public/js/app.js` | Boot, mode toggle, submit handlers, logout, show/hide modal vs shell, populate `current-user` |\n| `server/static.js` | `handleStatic(req, res, pathname) → boolean`: map `/` → `index.html`, safe file serve under `public/`, correct Content-Types |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/index.js` | After health + auth routes, call `handleStatic`; only then JSON 404. Do not alter health/auth status codes |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` | Optional: add `sendText(res, status, body, contentType)` used by static handler — keep `sendJson`/`readJson` behavior identical |\n| `test/server.test.js` (optional but recommended) | Assert `GET /` returns `200` and `text/html` containing `auth-modal` / `data-testid=\"auth-form\"`; assert `/api/health` still JSON |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/db.js` | Auth API owned by MARATHON-3; no logout endpoint in this task |\n| `start.sh`, `redis.conf` | Cluster bootstrap unchanged; static files need no extra process |\n| `timer.sh` | Harness |\n| Workspace/channel/message UI | MARATHON-22 / 23 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `public/index.html` + CSS skeleton with pinned hooks  \n2. `server/static.js` + wire `index.js` so `GET /` works on any node  \n3. `auth.js` API helpers  \n4. `app.js` boot / submit / logout flows  \n5. Manual check: register → token in localStorage → reload → still logged in → logout → login  \n\n### Parallelism\n- Frontend implementer owns `public/**` + static routing.\n- Backend auth already closed (MARATHON-3); do not block on MARATHON-4/5.\n- MARATHON-22 **architecture/implementation** depends on: authenticated shell mount, `huddle.token`, `huddle:auth` / `huddle:logout` events (or equivalent documented callbacks), and existing testids remaining stable.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| `GET /` HTML + static assets | QA; all SPA tasks |\n| `huddle.token` read/write/clear | MARATHON-22/23 fetch; MARATHON-18 WS `?token=` can read same key |\n| DOM testids / `#auth-modal` | QA automation |\n| Auth session events / `#app-shell` | MARATHON-22 three-pane; MARATHON-23 modals |\n\n### Build order\n- **Requires:** MARATHON-3 endpoints on the integrated head (present).\n- **Blocks:** Meaningful MARATHON-22 UI (declared dependent).\n- **Does not block:** MARATHON-4/5 backend work.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Owner |\n|-----|--------|\n| Workspaces, channels, three-pane, messages, their testids | MARATHON-22 |\n| Threads, reactions, settings modals | MARATHON-23 |\n| Profile PATCH UI | MARATHON-23 (API MARATHON-4) |\n| Server token revoke / logout API | New task if ever required |\n| Client-side router for deep links beyond `/` | MARATHON-22 if needed |\n\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\n\nNeighborhood scan (`server/`, `server/auth/`, `test/`, repo greps for `localStorage`, `auth-form`, `SPA`, `static`, `index.html`):\n\n| Finding | Why exc\n---DESCRIPTION---\nServe SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up/login form with visible validation errors; auto-login on success; logout/login restores workspace. Store token in localStorage huddle.token. Pin data-testid: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, current-user, logout-btn; ids auth-modal. Drivable at 1280x900.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":1050,"fileSize":62750,"path":"/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-worktrees-app-app-architect-1/agent-tools/33e06cea-2423-450c-b7d1-47b1dd4595df.txt","readRange":{"startLine":400,"endLine":1049},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-78e1c035-369e-467d-b69e-17750c0d2c3a-15\nfc_9c407e55-96f7-96c4-bb25-b0021178f9aa_1","startedAtMs":"1787428481177","completedAtMs":"1787428481250"},"model_call_id":"b9a0c0ee-9e46-4644-82ab-81a363f15c4c-5-vj8d","session_id":"659f50d8-61f9-4772-9eff-1622d4a8078e","timestamp_ms":1787428481302}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-78e1c035-369e-467d-b69e-17750c0d2c3a-14\nfc_9c407e55-96f7-96c4-bb25-b0021178f9aa_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"# Get epic notes properly and search for workspace contract\nloom data show MARATHON-1 --output json | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"NOTES:\", repr(d.get(\"notes\"))); print(\"design?\", bool(d.get(\"design\")))'\n# Find marathon contract / prompt with workspace specs\nrg -l -i 'join_mode|transfer_ownership|/api/workspaces' /work/ws /root 2>/dev/null | head -50\nfind /work/ws/app -type f 2>/dev/null | head -80\nls /work/ws/app 2>/dev/null\nls /work/ws/sessions/20260822-195343-app-architect-1--af982737/ 2>/dev/null | head\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-78e1c035-369e-467d-b69e-17750c0d2c3a-14\nfc_9c407e55-96f7-96c4-bb25-b0021178f9aa_0","simpleCommands":["loom","python3","rg","head","find","head","ls","ls","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-1"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-1 --output json"},{"name":"python3","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"NOTES:\", repr(d.get(\"notes\"))); print(\"design?\", bool(d.get(\"design\")))'"}],"fullText":"python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(\"NOTES:\", repr(d.get(\"notes\"))); print(\"design?\", bool(d.get(\"design\")))'"},{"name":"rg","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-l"},{"type":"word","value":"-i"},{"type":"raw_string","value":"'join_mode|transfer_ownership|/api/workspaces'"},{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws"},{"type":"word","value":"/root"}],"fullText":"rg -l -i 'join_mode|transfer_ownership|/api/workspaces' /work/w