llRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Extract full marathon grader spec text","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"659f50d8-61f9-4772-9eff-1622d4a8078e","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"python3 <<'PY'\nimport json,re\npath='/root/.cursor/projects/work-ws-app/agent-transcripts/5f883bf0-05a5-4cfa-8d9b-13de0430a3a7/5f883bf0-05a5-4cfa-8d9b-13de0430a3a7.jsonl'\nwith open(path) as fh:\n  for i,line in enumerate(fh):\n    d=json.loads(line)\n    role=d.get('role')\n    content=d.get('message',{}).get('content')\n    texts=[]\n    if isinstance(content,str):\n      texts=[content]\n    elif isinstance(content,list):\n      for c in content:\n        if isinstance(c,dict) and c.get('type')=='text':\n          texts.append(c['text'])\n    text='\\n'.join(texts)\n    if 'You have 4 hours' in text or ('API contract' in text and 'join_mode' in text):\n      print('LINE', i, 'role', role, 'len', len(text))\n      # write full text to file\n      open('/tmp/marathon-spec.txt','w').write(text)\n      print('wrote /tmp/marathon-spec.txt')\n      break\nPY\n# Find Workspaces section in the written file\nrg -n '^### |^## |WorkspaceObj|join_mode|transfer_ownership|ChannelObj' /tmp/marathon-spec.txt | head -80\n","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"LINE 4 role user len 20527\nwrote /tmp/marathon-spec.txt\n11:## API contract\n15:### REST conventions\n23:### Auth\n29:### Health\n33:### Profiles\n39:### Workspaces\n41:- `WorkspaceObj` carries at least `{id, slug, name, owner_id, join_mode}`. `join_mode` is `\"open\"` or `\"invite_only\"` and defaults to `\"open\"` on creation.\n46:- `PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}` — body any subset of `{name, join_mode}` — admin/owner only; `200 {workspace}` on success.\n47:- `PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}/members/{user_id}` — body `{role}`. Roles are `owner`, `admin`, `member`, `guest`. Promoting/demoting between `admin` and `member`/`guest` is owner-or-admin; admins cannot modify another admin or change `owner` (→ `403`); setting `role` to `owner` via PATCH is rejected (→ `400`) — use `transfer_ownership`. The current owner's role cannot be changed via PATCH (→ `403`).\n48:- `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/transfer_ownership` — body `{new_owner_id}`; owner-only. The target must already be an `admin` (otherwise `400`); on success the target becomes `owner` and the previous owner becomes `admin`.\n49:- **Open-workspace membership semantics**: when `join_mode == \"open\"`, any authenticated user can call `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` on a *public* channel in that workspace and is implicitly added as a `member` of the workspace (returns `200`). When `join_mode == \"invite_only\"`, non-members of the workspace get `403` on the channel-join unless they redeem a workspace invitation first.\n52:### Channels\n54:- `ChannelObj` carries at least `{id, workspace_id, name, is_private, is_dm, topic, is_archived}`. `topic` is a string up to 250 chars (longer → `400`) and defaults to `\"\"` on a freshly created channel — the `POST /channels` body does not carry a `description` field that auto-populates `topic`.\n64:### Messages, threads, reactions\n74:### DMs\n78:### Files\n85:### Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\n94:### User groups, invitations, roles\n101:### WebSocket\n108:### Performance\n112:### Frontend hooks\n121:### IRC gateway\n129:### Resilience\n134:### Prohibited approaches\n","stderr":"","executionTime":84,"interleavedOutput":"LINE 4 role user len 20527\nwrote /tmp/marathon-spec.txt\n11:## API contract\n15:### REST conventions\n23:### Auth\n29:### Health\n33:### Profiles\n39:### Workspaces\n41:- `WorkspaceObj` carries at least `{id, slug, name, owner_id, join_mode}`. `join_mode` is `\"open\"` or `\"invite_only\"` and defaults to `\"open\"` on creation.\n46:- `PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}` — body any subset of `{name, join_mode}` — admin/owner only; `200 {workspace}` on success.\n47:- `PATCH /api/workspaces/{slug}/members/{user_id}` — body `{role}`. Roles are `owner`, `admin`, `member`, `guest`. Promoting/demoting between `admin` and `member`/`guest` is owner-or-admin; admins cannot modify another admin or change `owner` (→ `403`); setting `role` to `owner` via PATCH is rejected (→ `400`) — use `transfer_ownership`. The current owner's role cannot be changed via PATCH (→ `403`).\n48:- `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/transfer_ownership` — body `{new_owner_id}`; owner-only. The target must already be an `admin` (otherwise `400`); on success the target becomes `owner` and the previous owner becomes `admin`.\n49:- **Open-workspace membership semantics**: when `join_mode == \"open\"`, any authenticated user can call `POST /api/channels/{id}/join` on a *public* channel in that workspace and is implicitly added as a `member` of the workspace (returns `200`). When `join_mode == \"invite_only\"`, non-members of the workspace get `403` on the channel-join unless they redeem a workspace invitation first.\n52:### Channels\n54:- `ChannelObj` carries at least `{id, workspace_id, name, is_private, is_dm, topic, is_archived}`. `topic` is a string up to 250 chars (longer → `400`) and defaults to `\"\"` on a freshly created channel — the `POST /channels` body does not carry a `description` field that auto-populates `topic`.\n64:### Messages, threads, reactions\n74:### DMs\n78:### Files\n85:### Search, slash commands, mentions, read state\n94:### User groups, invitations, roles\n101:### WebSocket\n108:### Performance\n112:### Frontend hooks\n121:### IRC gateway\n129:### Resilience\n134:### Prohibited approaches\n","localExecutionTimeMs":38},"isBackground":false},"description":"Extract full marathon grader spec text"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-e78c6e40-9410-489f-9b59-